    <node id="Santa Cruz Indians">
      <data key="d0">Santa Cruz Indians</data>
      <data key="d1">people</data>
      <data key="d2">The Santa Cruz Indians are an indigenous group that has been historically engaged in conflict against the Yucatecans since 1847.&lt;SEP&gt;The Santa Cruz Indians are an indigenous group in Yucatan, noted for holding two-thirds of the peninsula's fertile land since 1847.&lt;SEP&gt;The Santa Cruz Indians are another indigenous group referenced in relation to the territorial prohibitions against outsiders in their lands.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a838c08843884c0f3a0816d2b39bddaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eea61287f7c7aac52c315ee2cca003fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a980d05b1d871a902a88d111d028517</data>
