    <node id="Osiris">
      <data key="d0">Osiris</data>
      <data key="d1">deity</data>
      <data key="d2">Osiris is a significant deity in ancient Egyptian mythology, recognized as the king of the Amenti, where he adjudicates the fates of souls based on their earthly actions. He is intricately linked to the concepts of the afterlife and judgment, serving as a crucial figure in determining the passage of souls into the underworld.

Known as the son of the sky goddess Nut and the earth god Seb, Osiris is also acknowledged as the husband of Isis, adding a familial dimension to his character that enhances his role in mythological narratives. He is often depicted as a figure associated with death and resurrection, symbolizing the cycle of life and the hope for rebirth, which was central to ancient Egyptian beliefs.

Osiris's mythology includes a dramatic narrative where he was murdered by his brother Typho in a treacherous plot. This story is pivotal in Egyptian mythology, as it sets the stage for themes of resurrection, vengeance, and the eternal struggle between good and evil, exemplified by the conflicts between Osiris and Typho.

In addition to his mythological significance, Osiris is also referenced in religious rituals and practices, underscoring his role as a deity invoked for blessings and guidance, particularly in matters such as childbirth and other life transitions. His association with resurrection and the afterlife reinforces his status as a cornerstone of Egyptian religious thought, where he embodies the hope of immortality for all souls who lived righteous lives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa1a6047d3b960e8aa1f1e7a19add07e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f47d3b712e0953b518a70453701f3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e492003a084ec018b849a310a4e995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7dc5cd694c8e04568651d4ad21b8623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa4a04bbf52d96486efcb2e364d70456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0c76d7dabe39a2ef5714186a6126fc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1210480b5c05b18ce59cb21e5b063e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19630553a201da235d9c697d18820ca5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763623228</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Amenti">
      <data key="d0">Amenti</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Amenti refers to the realm over which Osiris presides, associated with the judgment of souls.&lt;SEP&gt;Amenti is referred to as the region of the West in Egyptian mythology, associated with the afterlife.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa1a6047d3b960e8aa1f1e7a19add07e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f47d3b712e0953b518a70453701f3ad</data>
