      <data key="d0">Moo</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Moo is a significant religious figure in the city of Izamal, worshipped with a shrine and held in high regard by pilgrims.&lt;SEP&gt;Moo is mentioned as the wife of Chaacmol in the mythological narrative involving familial conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Moo is the sister of Aac who marries their brother Chaacmol, guided by the legal customs of their society.&lt;SEP&gt;Moo is a character recognized as the Queen of Chichen, worshiped after her death at Izamal and a sister of Chacmol.&lt;SEP&gt;Moo is the wife and sister of Chaacmol, representing a figure of worship in Mayan culture often linked with the macaw.&lt;SEP&gt;Moo is depicted as a character who is warned by Cynocephalus of impending danger and is associated with domestic happiness.&lt;SEP&gt;Moo is depicted as a brother in the same mythological context as Aak and Chaacmol, involved in familial conflicts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-964858730c8a8dc2179e59d3cb07c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f47d3b712e0953b518a70453701f3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d60c6202de29d519891205dac45f966a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-002cf134516b6f6702e5dfec7413096b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e19091b4b68c6f4b29d836f6d5f11c0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e492003a084ec018b849a310a4e995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eea61287f7c7aac52c315ee2cca003fc</data>
