    <node id="Egyptians">
      <data key="d0">Egyptians</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Egyptians are referenced in context to cultural practices such as circumcision and religious rites.&lt;SEP&gt;The Egyptians are an ancient civilization known for their advancements in mathematics and architecture, including the construction of pyramids and their use of a septenary system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Egyptians are mentioned in the context of their writing system, which influenced the Mayan script.&lt;SEP&gt;The Egyptians are an ancient civilization noted for their cultural and religious practices and monumental architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;The Egyptians were an ancient civilization known for their advanced musical instruments, such as harps and flutes, and their contributions to music.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f65c2b617b2b75df32a484e145b034fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f83c27282913cff5172f6cf0dfa303eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e19091b4b68c6f4b29d836f6d5f11c0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa4a04bbf52d96486efcb2e364d70456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95fcd0021c644a0db5d36e039f705056&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-409162d6c592b356035008418a8c62af</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763626007</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sistrum">
      <data key="d0">Sistrum</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The sistrum was an instrument used in religious rites by both Egyptians and Mayas.&lt;SEP&gt;A sistrum is a musical instrument played during religious ceremonies, particularly by women in temples.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sistrum is a percussion instrument made of metal bars and used in religious performances.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sistrum is believed to be represented by the _menaaneim_, which is translated as cymbals in the English Bible.&lt;SEP&gt;The sistrum is an ancient musical instrument mentioned in the Hebrew context, associated with the term menaaneim.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sistrum is a musical instrument derived from Egypt, originally associated with the worship of Isis.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sistrum is an ancient Egyptian musical instrument shaken to produce sound, similar in function to the Frame described.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f65c2b617b2b75df32a484e145b034fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b991502e22e90fb761c5591cdca0b88e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d034b0ebc70d115fe140d386b94caa9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7da70d39d1688e8eb35f0af080c5cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5adf09848918f402d340b581ef777eb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aef18eb73774c5f975cff80e5f2ce51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
