    <node id="Mayab">
      <data key="d0">Mayab</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Mayab is the name thought to be derived from the absorbent quality of the soil in the region now known as Yucatan.&lt;SEP&gt;Mayab is associated with certain tribes of Yucatan and is referenced in relation to similar customs with Indian tribes.&lt;SEP&gt;Mayab refers to a region where similar burial customs and practices were carried out, akin to those of the Egyptians.&lt;SEP&gt;Mayab is a term referring to the region of the Mayan civilization, known for its cultural practices and historical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Mayab refers to a historical and cultural region associated with the Maya civilization, important for linguistic and scholarly studies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-90130c63183d6c112f655e298f1be97a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d60c6202de29d519891205dac45f966a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b991502e22e90fb761c5591cdca0b88e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eea61287f7c7aac52c315ee2cca003fc</data>
