    <node id="Online Distributed Proofreading Team">
      <data key="d0">Online Distributed Proofreading Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Online Distributed Proofreading Team is an organization dedicated to the proofreading, preparation, and digital archiving of literary works. This team plays a significant role in transforming images and resources provided by The Internet Archive/American Libraries into accessible e-text formats.

Their contributions extend to the production of various texts, including well-known works such as "Gallegher and Other Stories" and "Child's Health Primer." Specifically, the Online Distributed Proofreading Team is involved in projects like the preparation of the e-text for Scientific American Supplement No. 360, showcasing their commitment to enhancing literary accessibility through meticulous proofreading and formatting.

By utilizing page images and other resources from the Internet Archive, the team works to create accurate and thoroughly proofread digital versions of literary works, ensuring that these texts can be widely disseminated and preserved for future readers. Their efforts are integral to the broader movement of digitizing literature and making it available to a global audience.&lt;SEP&gt;The Online Distributed Proofreading Team is responsible for producing the text utilizing resources from the Bibliotheque nationale de France.&lt;SEP&gt;The Online Distributed Proofreading Team is responsible for producing the file from images provided by The Internet Archive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53318967e1e0c7a354ac926405083d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37436bbfc5c51f8d3f5eadaa7be7704&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e35b84d5e9534312cd2edd202ad1eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c7457182fd8c984b4b4d5b338a0a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ab7ad03b323561e72dda983ec2d3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4861f1f36dbc583ebdad31a4a80a0aad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c92bbb1fd6ed4d39b3fbf9331923c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73c170ba2d6f65788ae52ee29483e59d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c680d4e3c6d389236c61c1ca4a429d6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763627442</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Internet Archive">
      <data key="d0">The Internet Archive</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Internet Archive is a library that provides access to various resources, including the images used for the book’s production.&lt;SEP&gt;The Internet Archive is a non-profit digital library that provides access to various digital media, including page images used for "Dandy Dick."&lt;SEP&gt;The Internet Archive is a non-profit digital library that offers free public access to a vast collection of digital content, including scanned books and texts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Internet Archive provided images that contributed to the creation of "An Unsentimental Journey Through Cornwall."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53318967e1e0c7a354ac926405083d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f87fddca66673ee08a52eb11ebbc03dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b99d32a6c4077b81dac5436dc1d07de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c680d4e3c6d389236c61c1ca4a429d6</data>
