      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Thebes is the capital of upper Egypt during the XVIII dynasty and known in hieroglyphs as NO or NA-AMUN, the mansion of Amun.&lt;SEP&gt;Thebes is mentioned as a historical location related to power and grandeur, used in the context of the speaker's poetic reflections.&lt;SEP&gt;Thebes is mentioned in the context of war and poetry, suggesting its historical significance in narratives of conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Thebes is an ancient city in Egypt, known for its significant archaeological sites, including tombs containing representations of musical instruments.</data>
