    <node id="Noah Carter">
      <data key="d0">Noah Carter</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Noah Carter is a prominent sprinter known for setting a new record in the 100m sprint at the World Athletics Championship. His athletic prowess has garnered significant attention, establishing him as a notable figure in the world of track and field.

In addition to his accomplishments as an athlete, there are references to another aspect of Noah Carter's identity, possibly as a character in a narrative context. This Noah Carter expresses deep feelings of torment and affection towards someone, highlighting a complex emotional landscape filled with love and rivalry. He laments not being received by his mistress, which adds to his sense of anguish, and he compares himself to a wealthy rival, underlining the themes of competition and unrequited feelings.

Overall, Noah Carter embodies both exceptional athletic talent and a dramatic emotional depth in narrative form, with his duality reflecting both physical achievements in sports and intricate personal experiences in storytelling.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah Carter is a sprinter who set a new record in the 100m sprint at the World Athletics Championship.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah Carter is a character who is depicted singing and interacting with musical instruments and other characters in a social setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah Carter is a character referenced in the context of activities undertaken on St. Michael's Mount.</data>
