    <node id="Unit">
      <data key="d0">Unit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Unit refers to the group of individuals including officers and soldiers traveling aboard the ship.&lt;SEP&gt;The unit refers to a group that includes British and Russian individuals during their time together in a foreign country.&lt;SEP&gt;The Unit is referred to as the medical group working together to care for patients and face challenges during wartime.&lt;SEP&gt;The Unit refers to the group of medical staff and their collective efforts and experiences during a military campaign.&lt;SEP&gt;The unit refers to the group of Serbian soldiers and personnel that Dr. Inglis worked with during their journey.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72d185691764f4ca25d0dd5b47c77ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7229deb809f43a17e844ef4f20769c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5d2c15127c77eb0e9171d1fb1a5e1e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ce0ef9057b54adcabf7cff5d8d40d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7f3fc74bc960c00595a6361c3449b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed6d0588bb9562256b939c28fa258ac</data>
