      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mrs. Inglis is a mother who writes accounts of her experience with her daughter, Elsie, and her observations regarding family life and travels in India.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Inglis is the strong mother figure who influenced her children's spiritual life and education.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Inglis was the mother in the Inglis family who had to make sacrifices during Mr. Inglis's time in India.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Inglis is portrayed as a maternal figure exhibiting skepticism towards certain events and guidance for her daughter.</data>
