      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Glasgow is the city where Elsie Inglis resided while studying at the Medical School and where she took the examination for the Triple Qualification.&lt;SEP&gt;Glasgow is the city where women students faced opposition to mixed classes in medical education.&lt;SEP&gt;Glasgow is a city where clinical work was completed and examinations were passed by Elsie.&lt;SEP&gt;Glasgow is referenced as a city with one of the largest out-patient departments in the kingdom and a place related to medical student practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Glasgow is a city mentioned where Elsie Inglis communicated with her father about women's rights in 1891.&lt;SEP&gt;Glasgow is the city where the meeting with Sir George Beatson took place.&lt;SEP&gt;Glasgow is a city where the ship was previously docked for repairs before the voyage.</data>
