    <node id="Serbia">
      <data key="d0">Serbia</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Serbia is mentioned as one of the locations where Dr. Elsie demonstrated her quality of self-command during retreats.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbia is one of the countries where the Scottish Women’s Hospitals operated during wartime.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbia is a nation that experienced significant hardships during the war, with a strong desire for independence and unity among its people.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbia is the country where the Scottish Women’s Unit was stationed and where they attempted to assist the local population during the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbia is the nation referred to as enduring significant hardship and tribulation during the conflicts discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbia is a country mentioned in the context of military operations and retreats during the war.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbia is a country represented at the funeral of Elsie Inglis, symbolizing her commitment and connection to its people.</data>
