    <node id="Elsie Inglis">
      <data key="d0">Elsie Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Elsie Inglis was a pioneering figure in the field of medicine and a dedicated advocate for women's rights. She is notable for her substantial contributions to women's access to medical education and practice, having been associated with the Medical College for Women in Edinburgh. As a female medical student and later a physician, Inglis worked at the New Hospital for Women, where she furthered her training among a staff of female doctors. Her commitment to women's causes was not only evident in her professional life but also in her political activism.

Inglis played a significant role in the suffrage movement, recognized for her leadership and dedication to advocating for women's rights. She was particularly influential in establishing medical units during times of conflict, reflecting her dual commitment to healthcare and women's empowerment. Her humanitarian efforts were particularly pronounced during the war, where she became known as a heroic figure for her devotion to medical care, especially in Serbia. Inglis contributed significantly to nursing and medical aid during the Typhus Epidemic in Serbia and was instrumental in supporting the Serbian army during this crisis.

Throughout her life, Elsie Inglis founded a nursing home in Edinburgh and participated actively in various causes that aimed to enhance the role of women in medicine and society. She was recognized not only for her professional achievements but also for her personal integrity and honor, embodying the spirit of compassionate service. She recently passed away, leaving behind a legacy as a noble lady who made indelible contributions during her lifetime, particularly in connecting Scotland and Serbia through her humanitarian efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a2678b978dddcb10f74685afcc33826d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64db1dd7d0712bd0b11ae20de546f3e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1105db92c26143035157a3a806604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8dce7295514b70b9ccac7f7f258d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa2387fc90852af29634d0f93b3c46b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fc5bb98f8d283a62db5e74bbfa9071&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b38719c302bfd7a79cb6bf09c381277c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510929c91e3f9a3e013feb10138683ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-795bd02c45b0e38f40d224f9f9752778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-615fd00e3494a05f5434700852bd4911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6b3f825b0114b7c33343abfedda35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ab1577aaf007918da08d1e5f32fbf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6540245da04893916f916cbd8b74aa3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd87c44c3eeac386b02307ff6bf32d8</data>
