      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mrs. Fawcett is an advocate who obtained funding for representing women's work at the Chicago Exhibition.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Fawcett was recognized as a leader among the women suffrage societies, guiding their efforts in the political arena.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Fawcett is an associate of Dr. Inglis who recognized and documented her contributions and challenges in gaining support for women's hospital initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Fawcett is an individual who documented Dr. Inglis's experiences, highlighting her challenges with the War Office.</data>
