    <node id="War Office">
      <data key="d0">War Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The War Office is the government department that Dr. Inglis interacted with to assist her patient’s family after the war.&lt;SEP&gt;The War Office is the former government department responsible for the administration of the British Army and military affairs during the war.&lt;SEP&gt;The War Office is the official military department that initially refused Dr. Inglis's offers of service for women's hospitals during the war.&lt;SEP&gt;The War Office is a government department involved in military operations and logistics during wartime, referenced in the context of Dr. Inglis seeking support.&lt;SEP&gt;The War Office is a governmental body involved in military communications during the events described.</data>
