    <node id="Dr. Elsie Inglis">
      <data key="d0">Dr. Elsie Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dr. Elsie Inglis is recognized for her noble character and significant contributions, symbolizing the spirit of her nation.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis was a leader in the movement for women's suffrage and played a significant role in the Scottish Women’s Hospitals.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis was a pioneering physician and advocate for women's rights, known for her significant contributions to medical services for women and her political activism.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis was a key figure during the war period, qualified to play a significant role among the Allied nations.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis was a prominent figure providing aid during the Serbian typhus epidemic and was commemorated for her services by the Serbian nation.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis is a dedicated individual known for her unwavering commitment to humanitarian work, particularly for the Serbian people during wartime.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce963d77a022a25ba3a2d2ad400fa56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b818ac8f082f95c6bdf7a8460dd50f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c858db77dc3126e37cd384f8634ecffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37436bbfc5c51f8d3f5eadaa7be7704&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9fec82f84d40eb54a3c1a3965739403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64ab42f17996dafda93ff20305420aba</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
