    <node id="Elsie">
      <data key="d0">Elsie</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Elsie is a multifaceted character known for her vibrant personality and strong will throughout her life. Described as a temperamental baby with a lively curiosity and a penchant for laughter, she stands out in the memories shared by those around her. As a child, Elsie's imaginative play captured the hearts of her peers, and she later excelled academically, embodying a spirit of service and leadership in her school environment. Notably, she demonstrated extraordinary courage by actively seeking permission for her classmates to enjoy the gardens of Charlotte Square and contributing to the Edina magazine.

In her journey towards adulthood, Elsie emerged as a politically engaged individual, advocating for women's suffrage and expressing her views on social matters. Her engagement in intense discussions showcases her strong opinions and dedication to advancing women's rights. Elsie's letters, filled with reflections on personal experiences and observations, reveal her thoughtful nature and her role as an inspirer of friendship among those around her.

As she pursued her education, Elsie faced challenges in the medical field, where she articulated the struggles encountered by women seeking medical degrees. She planned to rent a hall for a dispensary and continued her studies in Midwifery in Dublin, demonstrating her commitment to healthcare. During wartime, she served as a medical professional, writing heartfelt letters home about her experiences in the hospitals and her concerns for the well-being of orderlies and fellow workers.

Her correspondence also highlights her affectionate relationship with her niece and her deep feelings for her family, providing a personal touch that enhances the understanding of her character. Overall, Elsie embodies bravery, dedication, and empathy, leaving a lasting impact through her actions and the connections she fostered throughout her life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72d185691764f4ca25d0dd5b47c77ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb6a025623f47200c8c812a059793950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb473cc1631a419d818447e583a4e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c89e82ea0a483e5673a0449dbed190&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4dc7c9f3044941df1985ca230c24ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3414d2b797b5a6e968d2553d8c3ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a495d646117c26bb32b54340d258cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81ae10df52932fd952fbc03a861bd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2462ff70f1dbd30f8a4b0b4d73c23c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f3981fcd4c2dbb0ee85b59b7739f90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7643380e1b94787722b1984480288f4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9951e0a4df9c638e61728ec9f7bb04ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95ca1798f1fdc6104abc9bed1cf52f5</data>
