    <node id="Ireland">
      <data key="d0">Ireland</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Ireland is a focal point in the discussion of Home Rule and political reforms being debated in the Parliament.&lt;SEP&gt;Ireland is mentioned as the origin of a tour made in 1789, contributing to the cultural context of the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Ireland is mentioned as the homeland of the fairy-folk and serves as a backdrop for the good hermit's story.&lt;SEP&gt;Ireland is mentioned as the home that could potentially be bought by Michael O'Shaughnessy, indicating its cultural and geographical significance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Ireland is a country with a rich history in the tradition of playing the bagpipe, mentioned in poetry and prose dating back to the tenth century.</data>
