    <node id="David Inglis">
      <data key="d0">David Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">David Inglis is the son of Alexander Inglis and is noted for being Dux of his class and later went to India as a writer for the East India Company.&lt;SEP&gt;David Inglis is a writer who served in India during the Mahratta War and was involved in significant negotiations under the Treaty of Bassein in 1803.&lt;SEP&gt;David Inglis is mentioned as Elsie's father, writing to his son on his marriage in 1845, expressing deep interest and hopes for his son's future.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1f01e511989b4651de0b56333122230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2462ff70f1dbd30f8a4b0b4d73c23c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c9efbd12b4170d1e884f967c9273e05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
