    <node id="Gibraltar">
      <data key="d0">Gibraltar</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Gibraltar is referenced as one of the locations from which letters were received from aunts of David Inglis, indicating the family’s broad connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Gibraltar is the territory ceded to England following the peace of Utrecht.&lt;SEP&gt;Gibraltar is mentioned as a site for a secret arrangement concerning the supply of provisions to its garrison.&lt;SEP&gt;Gibraltar is a British Overseas Territory, directly opposite Ceuta, known for its rock and the presence of monkeys.&lt;SEP&gt;Gibraltar is a location from where ordnance was furnished for the forts in Rabat.&lt;SEP&gt;Gibraltar is a strategic location mentioned in connection with British naval power.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1f01e511989b4651de0b56333122230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1b63bc45a96581a48ba223c8d48c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ee1dd105b3b5398ba93ec7c92e6dc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c31ea51debe67089624a49cd283a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0feaae427cf9b154a9a737a238afba</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
