      <data key="d0">G. H.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The G. H. is an abbreviation for a publication that discusses changes in education and their impact on women's rights.&lt;SEP&gt;G. H. is characterized by a belief that changes will lead to women's suffrage and participation in the Church.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e1105db92c26143035157a3a806604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f3981fcd4c2dbb0ee85b59b7739f90</data>
