      <data key="d1">group</data>
      <data key="d2">The children of the Inglis family played a crucial role in their family dynamics and experiences in India.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are referenced as a demographic in the context of muscle development through play and physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are highlighted as individuals who gradually take on the responsibility of caring for themselves as they grow older.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are individuals who play outdoors and require regular washing to remove dirt and waste from their skin.&lt;SEP&gt;The children are present at a family gathering, where they share a meal with the narrator.</data>
