      <data key="d2">Asaph is Angeline's husband who is encouraged to continue his studies and pursue a career in academia.&lt;SEP&gt;Asaph is one of Angeline Hall's children and is humorously mentioned regarding his name spelling game.&lt;SEP&gt;Asaph is mentioned as the little son who was taken to the saloon by his mother.&lt;SEP&gt;Asaph is a family member mentioned in the letter, receiving updates from C. A. S. Hall.</data>
