    <node id="Elisha Cook">
      <data key="d0">Elisha Cook</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Elisha Cook is the husband of Huldah Cook, who together initiated the westward migration from Ellington.&lt;SEP&gt;Elisha Cook is referenced as the father of Electa Cook and is associated with the Black River Country during the War of 1812.&lt;SEP&gt;Elisha Cook is Angeline’s uncle, associated with the punishment methods used in the local school.&lt;SEP&gt;Elisha Cook is a character who passed away in the summer of 1841, marking a significant event in Lady Angeline's life.&lt;SEP&gt;Elisha Cook is referenced as a relative of Professor Hall who shared childhood experiences with Thomas Sabin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eae53fd856d28203afb9cca734e561df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ada5b526daab8bb42bced4bd5ee488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-761dc75dfaa658aca91981a9ec83d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14b5f22393f8a2efe13082af4bcd332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdaa7c773b77f31c7a3cbf9cdb813d4</data>
