    <node id="Mr. Hall">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Hall</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. Hall is Angeline Stickney's lover, who corresponds with her about their feelings and future plans, showing a deep emotional connection.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Hall refers to Asaph Hall in the context of disagreements about women's rights and domestic responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Hall is referred to as a scholar who is gaining recognition in his science field and has published work in the Astronomical Journal.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Hall is a character who is involved in various communications and professional developments throughout the text, including letters regarding appointments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c7f5587c120cd6b77ca7604ffa3373d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7cbaacbda1b565d7c16cf842522b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc55b5be1d859abaa2b489bc942a9fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9edfe0fb8fa0058acfbbae0026363f1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ba2e01ff70de4541cc6b1d7ee24441</data>
