    <node id="Virgil">
      <data key="d0">Virgil</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Virgil is a classical author whose works were studied by Angeline Stickney during her time at New York Central College.&lt;SEP&gt;Virgil is a respected Roman poet known for his literary contributions, which reflect the moral sentiments of his time.&lt;SEP&gt;Virgil is a famous Roman poet who introduced himself as Tityrus in his first Eclogue.&lt;SEP&gt;Virgil is mentioned as a poet who reflects on personal experiences involving property disputes during Augustus's rule.&lt;SEP&gt;Virgil is a classical author who provides commentary on various subjects including mythology and history in their texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Virgil is a Roman poet known for his literary contributions and his relationship with Æmilius Macer.</data>
