    <node id="McGrawville">
      <data key="d0">McGrawville</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">McGrawville is a notable location in Cortland County, New York, primarily associated with various educational experiences and historical figures. It is prominently mentioned in connection with Angeline Stickney, who chose to further her education in this town, where she also met her future husband. McGrawville is home to New York Central College, further underscoring its significance as an educational hub.

In the narratives surrounding Angeline and her cousin, Mary Gilman, McGrawville emerges as a setting for their boarding arrangements and social visits, illustrating the personal connections and educational journeys experienced there. The location is depicted as a gathering point for friendships and family, where Angeline would visit friends and relatives after an encounter with Mr. Hall did not go as planned.

Additionally, Asaph Hall 3rd is linked to McGrawville, having moved there to pursue both academic and manual labor opportunities. The town is also historically tied to other figures, such as Col. A. J. Warner, an associate of Asaph Hall during the Civil War. 

Overall, McGrawville is characterized as a significant site of education, personal development, and social interaction during a transformative period in the lives of those associated with it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-59c37387ba8758c27d10bbea3fdf809b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cc551f9bef83bf4d019c7da7b576d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bed6738b6d7b4e2dc22c8db0e48f9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e509d5b8e0fa267a06304105affc4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e24a8d13114f74ad6389fc6ea6b12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3573c74971fb594d0887556481e6476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7b901adf8679c3923b1589b8a4a5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9edfe0fb8fa0058acfbbae0026363f1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ff5fd31602189a7d4e036b27dcf956b</data>
