      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mrs. Hall refers to Angeline Hall, particularly when discussing women's rights and contributions to the movement for bloomers in Boston.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Hall is a character who corresponds with her sister Mary and discusses her husband’s scholarly achievements.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Hall is a character who personifies virtue and devotion, attending to her family's needs while engaging in community service.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Hall is a character sensitive to beauty and dedicated to cultivating her garden, showing great love for her family.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Hall is characterized by her devotion to her husband and her enthusiasm for his work, despite not fully comprehending it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b7cbaacbda1b565d7c16cf842522b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc55b5be1d859abaa2b489bc942a9fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93cf4b36f5828cc09fb907dbf61daf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdaa7c773b77f31c7a3cbf9cdb813d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79b9fa6a515afb504b93b48cecc495d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f5587c120cd6b77ca7604ffa3373d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ba2e01ff70de4541cc6b1d7ee24441</data>
