    <node id="Cider">
      <data key="d0">Cider</data>
      <data key="d1">product</data>
      <data key="d2">Cider is a beverage mentioned as part of a package sent from Sister Mary to Angeline Hall.&lt;SEP&gt;Cider is a beverage that can be boiled and used as an ingredient in pies and sauces.&lt;SEP&gt;Cider is a liquid produced from apples, which undergoes processing to remove impurities and enhance clarity.&lt;SEP&gt;Cider is a fermented drink made from apple juice that also contains alcohol, formed through the fermentation process after pressing the apples.&lt;SEP&gt;Cider is an alcoholic drink made from the fermentation of apple juice and is considered a weaker liquor compared to distilled products.&lt;SEP&gt;Cider is a fermented beverage produced from apples, which contains a lower alcohol content compared to distilled spirits.&lt;SEP&gt;Cider is a beverage made from crushed apples, which can become detrimental when alcohol begins to form in it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d483764952d7db72ab6b8abd0b9b597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04ccd4dad326e3c82f9a671aff50b17e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7506d04f954ae2d1cb0ed256f5c0e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d170d1426917b3639e7243e4aade782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
