      <data key="d0">Sugar</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sugar is a valuable product derived from a tree mentioned in the text, highlighting the tree's usefulness.&lt;SEP&gt;Sugar is a carbohydrate present in fruit juices that can be converted into alcohol during fermentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Sugar is a sweet carbohydrate produced from the transformation of starch during the sprouting phase of grains.&lt;SEP&gt;Sugar is a carbohydrate that contributes to fat formation and provides energy for bodily functions.</data>
