    <node id="Philadelphia">
      <data key="d0">Philadelphia</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Philadelphia is a city where the narrator temporarily stays while seeking to form a class.&lt;SEP&gt;Philadelphia is the city where the flouring mill operates and where significant cost analyses of steam, coal, and water consumption took place.&lt;SEP&gt;Philadelphia is a city where Girard College, an early marble building, is located.&lt;SEP&gt;Philadelphia is the city where Gallegher resides and performs various activities related to his role as an office boy.&lt;SEP&gt;Philadelphia is a city referenced as the destination for the stranger Gallegher pursues.&lt;SEP&gt;Philadelphia is a city that serves as a setting for the criminal activities and the murder investigation discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Philadelphia is the city located four miles to the south of the scene, contributing a faint glow to the night sky.</data>
