    <node id="Vorticella">
      <data key="d0">Vorticella</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Vorticella is a character who is associated with the publishing of critical opinions and is perceived as having a powerful personality, influencing others.&lt;SEP&gt;Vorticella is identified as an author who wrote a book titled 'The Channel Islands, with Notes and an Appendix' and is characterized for her societal opinions and literary aspirations.&lt;SEP&gt;Vorticella is a character who expresses her opinions on criticism and authorship, discussing the reception of her book and the critiques it has received.&lt;SEP&gt;Vorticella is a type of creature that is referenced in relation to the concept of vanity and disfiguration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ead820aa22844313f5dfed6efdc81ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-625804364e635f703f6cec4378f9af4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fee473d0cd24b2b054fd03b290013c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b0a545773b8336ab8625e557443eba8</data>
