    <node id="Merman">
      <data key="d0">Merman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Merman is a character who started as a young conveyancer and became involved in periodical writing and studying moral and physical science.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a character who engages in intellectual discourse and holds strong beliefs about social origins and historical perspectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a character who is determined to gather knowledge and confront his adversary, Grampus, while preparing a comprehensive argument.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a figure who is criticized for his shallow understanding of philological and archaeological studies and becomes notorious due to his disputes with Grampus.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is characterized as a plagiarist and a theorist with eccentric ideas, struggling with the criticism of his work and the consequences of his controversial views.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a character who feels ill-used by the world and experiences disappointment in his relationships and societal standing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0caba7a3455a33871464a9439e236182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbf078c5fa58ff6dbd05d3e173932f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15731bb06f5468be78ed2b36a5ef8f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f5219425f0dd684e1c14ee102afdc4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5</data>
