    <node id="Grampus">
      <data key="d0">Grampus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Grampus is an author whose work is described as epoch-making and was influential in Merman's life.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is a character whose book is challenged by Merman, who believes Grampus is mistaken in his views.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is described as an eminent adversary, notable for his expertise and authority, particularly in erudition.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is an individual who critiques Merman's work and possesses significant knowledge that he uses to defend his views on the Magicodumbras and Zuzumotzis.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is referenced as a competitor to Merman, whose work Merman claims to appropriate ideas from him, reflecting academic jealousy.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is a figure whose ideas were later respected, contrasting with Merman’s perceived impracticality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0caba7a3455a33871464a9439e236182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbf078c5fa58ff6dbd05d3e173932f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15731bb06f5468be78ed2b36a5ef8f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f5219425f0dd684e1c14ee102afdc4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5</data>
