    <node id="Society">
      <data key="d0">Society</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Society encapsulates the community context in which various characters, including Merman and Lentulus, navigate their relationships and aspirations.&lt;SEP&gt;Society is mentioned as an entity that is not solely dependent on a minority for growth and can include broad participation.&lt;SEP&gt;Society is a community of individuals who are interconnected and affected by shared morals and intellect.&lt;SEP&gt;The Society is referenced as an entity making decisions about the care of the baby, indicating a governing or influential role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Society is an entity mentioned by the burglar, indicating an organization that provided support or conditions influencing the burglar's situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Society is an organization that influences the burglar's ability to earn money and travel, as mentioned in the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-022b8d49df0a9b3198a3827e7ca1f148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b35cd39246570e8cc51cc541f1b742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dc1b3bed5fc2f671459f1471fbaec93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7196deec353a5499b089c79c1d6267a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7617cb6098946fe96b78f351798eb36</data>
