      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Civilisation">
      <data key="d0">Civilisation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Civilisation refers to the advanced state of human social development, which can be easily threatened during crises.&lt;SEP&gt;Civilisation is discussed as a transformed state of tribal existence, critiqued in the context of its contrasts to Jewish identity.&lt;SEP&gt;Civilisation refers to the state of society with advanced cultural development, mentioned in the context of the travelers returning to it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96c97616301428800d67230455b99e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66a11e3fdc0678e4dcf84b4d05935cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-529c2631117811cb886077fba9841146</data>
