    <node id="Romans">
      <data key="d0">Romans</data>
      <data key="d1">people</data>
      <data key="d2">Romans are referenced as a dominant historical power that exerted control and influence over the Jewish people, leading to conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;The Romans are referenced in relation to cultural practices such as dancing, which was discouraged among them.&lt;SEP&gt;The Romans were an ancient civilization that adopted musical instruments from various cultures, including the Etruscans and Greeks.&lt;SEP&gt;Romans refer to the people of ancient Rome who conquered North Africa and referred to indigenous tribes as Moors and Berbers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Romans were a powerful civilization that gained control of Africa from the Phoenicians and later faced invasions from various groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Romans were an ancient civilization known for their extensive empire and cultural achievements, influencing regions of Europe and North Africa.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be50f96825f2130199a486741f5ef6c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7feca07c634684d8111b02a41fcae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f52bfe54d47067a25b5b0c44706763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cbd510e5f844be534e59040af85f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3a1103e1d6efafaf897eb994dbaa44</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
