    <node id="Bruin">
      <data key="d0">Bruin</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Bruin is a bear character who exhibits a range of social and emotional behaviors, often participating in conversations and activities that highlight his depth and personality. He is portrayed as kind-hearted and caring, frequently assisting friends like Toto and the Crow in their various endeavors, including efforts to help a sick master. His interactions showcase his concern for others, as he expresses affection and support for characters such as Baldhead and exhibits protective behavior towards Pigeon Pretty.

Despite his large size, Bruin often displays a sense of humility and self-consciousness about his appearance, desiring to be less frightening. He engages in playful activities, such as attempting jumping tricks, and is involved in humorous situations, including a memorable incident where he accidentally causes chaos by sitting on a custard pie. His playful, yet thoughtful nature is also evident during leisurely moments, such as playing backgammon with the Hermit, where he reflects on luck, winter, and leisure activities.

Bruin's role as a mediator is highlighted in occurrences where he navigates conflicts, such as intervening during confrontations or suggesting behavioral changes to others, showcasing his authoritative yet compassionate demeanor. He readily engages in conversations about past family stories and memories with Toto, and he is active in helping with preparations for social gatherings, contributing to the lively atmosphere with his humorous nature. 

Overall, Bruin is depicted as a multifaceted character with both comical and gentle traits, embodying emotions ranging from playful to despairing, and continually striving to support his friends and contribute positively to their interactions. His essence combines a sense of playfulness with a commitment to kindness and community, making him a beloved figure in his narrative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab5a2da379766b69f7bf3153cb0f2c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3e57d404581a83d442385fc9e650dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b84f4e93e76fa38e1e70383218e0788b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60d4926e5d4ac6ded55aa7e91fca4c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e172b463b651297a4b51743b0d92c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2d18b61665def22c8f765c51d5d1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02eb71062b272bf903fae543230157a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a372fe9a6fbcab1dde3e0bf0d1e5c883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a12948208c13074a50572b428e264d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e6b02f461263b84f5b3f2aada29ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771de78b693da0d88850589600bace97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-586a7611f02b1deff7ed6b0d6bdd65af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a69e187e3b23aa9bc91e07518123699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c686441b3937cff685f4451d4cd9685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-741254ee870941013c032a0acf8e5a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-216931ed57c995344f647fe87af541bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd1416667b27714cea22c448d2c7894&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c0ae512a1dc43eac54573c59477cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6778bb1c4c17f23f0cc54a25751bc2f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c5e6743d54bfa5b3f1b9509aacd347e</data>
