      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Eugenius refers to the spurious volumes associated with Sterne's works, mentioned in the context of Bode's translation.&lt;SEP&gt;Eugenius is likely a character associated with the original narrative text that Bode is translating, serving as a point of contrast to Bode's translations.&lt;SEP&gt;Eugenius is the character whose continuation of Yorick’s Journey is mentioned as being translated by Bode.&lt;SEP&gt;Eugenius is a character who narrates an episode regarding M’lle Laborde and relates to the education of Tristram.&lt;SEP&gt;Eugenius is identified as a recipient of one of the letters included in the anonymous collection, indicating a connection to Bode.</data>
