    <node id="Sterne">
      <data key="d0">Sterne</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sterne is a prominent English author best known for his influential works, particularly "Tristram Shandy" and "The Sentimental Journey." His narrative powers and unique style, marked by digressions and a playful engagement with readers, have garnered recognition in both England and Germany, where his literary contributions sparked discussions among critics and fellow writers. Sterne's explorations of sentiment and emotional experiences are especially evident in "The Sentimental Journey," which has been cited as an inspiration for various translations and adaptations in German literature.

Critics have noted that Sterne's works, including the aforementioned titles, have impacted figures like Herder, Hamann, Goethe, and Schummel, showcasing a blend of humor, sentiment, and unconventional narrative techniques. His storytelling is characterized by whimsical elements and a distinctive treatment of themes like master-servant relationships, which have influenced the perception of these dynamics in literature. Despite his literary genius, reactions to Sterne's work have varied, with some critiques highlighting a perceived manipulation of readers' sentiments and a decline in moral character.

Sterne's narratives have not only inspired adaptations and imitations but have also prompted scrutiny regarding borrowing and originality, particularly concerning literary figures like Lessing and Ferriar. His letters, published posthumously in 1775, further illuminate his emotional and whimsical writing style, contributing to a complex legacy that is often discussed within the context of the sentimental movement.

In Germany, Sterne's influence was acknowledged as part of the literary currents of his time, contrasting with a less favorable reception in England. His work has been described as a significant point of reference for numerous writers, reflecting the widespread impact of his narrative style and thematic choices. Overall, Sterne remains a pivotal figure in the study of literature, exemplifying the intersections of sentimentality, humor, and innovative narrative techniques that have shaped literary traditions across cultures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55bae40ef4db541cd7f64d0262ea22a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04dbd687736802afbe261266a5f387e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939e417a7df4f7cc2019f7a0a8f2b15a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42f3a2f0a754041c29f091e82271385c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e651b63e26f770b43ffddb9d79cab59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10af28895017a86626bcf11657f1ec8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb9f823daea4acf22b2dce0ec0b834ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea440613a1c400f54c6088d2b80f02cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e48c21535b598ccc004c7edbc7f2c216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7f1d14d418ffd32ee04aefb91e7331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3dcaffe826a353c7b1a0eff516a2419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58d87bc060205995efa9baf4bddb1a07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3633c2240cf930228d1d94b3be682bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-483dfdb84cf847447a77aecaac7cb8a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c3f247ede6e2e4cbb7778c1b56fd58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302bb08717ae1ac7bbe814edbfc98875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22d20d40b43b3d2c1dbb21d56b7f2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb3d3d51e372c48bb1c3585adf76c5fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42cef61a79d34e5bcf885a966963554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f7d055c140a23788c7b5cad8fb7948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fffe095b624cf5296e4dd35470f940d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d15e55fa6a03a4ae9a73fae85bc97ec2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30eda9443e1378b86c375a7fe5c0eb06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12e58d009015748875e7d97f6b72f688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b57f8b57daf11b165b8852ab7e62eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dcb2da270a1bb0417354dcf23b9656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559b00cb6dc756396bfc420ba8cc5cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-073c32eb7cfcec94cf8952d9901d1c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33391ef46d6fc8b213e88db6e3b4648e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-573f9ee936a1b21e04721d34c3cc59f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11d94df1514c9134e03d19c4744e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835b2b68b00b2bd674ad666036ecbc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b527db1f11e9eeff8a9a251b1ec766ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bba52ca6db0e619b578b5cf52494e654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84307003973059440e3b98bafcdbef48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6830a00197a03b02eae670e7f2e9ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9514ef0c01ef6384fdf0e7549eeccb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c29ec3cd76c13c7da9bd30bfc253b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c128264faa77a054077d4c6bfd355759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bed52ff145a82972c1126c22e4c660b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4a45157e34604d157e56225b4b8622b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f99047222f973cdfa74a4aaa41bc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b979cdc44cde067d90763ef953998ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e70d2514d488605a1422b519a75a4fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad7eb91ef19d9479c183ea94881f5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ccff1ea6ecc4a7b158250715bcedc0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f84f8d10490e85138ed83f5d3bbf9fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1253429524c402a0bdec28c9d9e74654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e50573346c99fdc27483fe15f2cd8f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-732304afc34a1c4dbb7b84c2c485e530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eb63434ade7863dbb529206940c54f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ecb8725d9b49ee2bda6cf5f19b07499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9c0013c86c9a2d0424cec3204472c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56a19306fc0bdd6d75f01267c814f30c</data>
