      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Jacobi is an individual criticized for publicly printing a private letter and later expressed shame about his actions regarding the snuff-box fad.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacobi is mentioned as an intermediary who describes a sentimental family regarding the treatment of doves.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacobi is a contemporaneous writer referenced for his correspondence and influence concerning literary discussions of Sterne and Yorick.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacobi is an author whose works, including Winterreise, were influenced by Yorick, and whose reception has been shaped by contemporary critics.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacobi is mentioned in context as a character whose failure to be democratic is contrasted with the traveler's request for Pumper.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacobi is mentioned in relation to his remarks about Sterne's literary influence within his preface to Winterreise.</data>
