    <node id="Lessing">
      <data key="d0">Lessing</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lessing is a prominent literary figure and German scholar recognized for his contributions to the discourse surrounding literature and cultural thought. He expressed significant admiration for the works of Laurence Sterne, notably showing an early interest in Sterne’s "Tristram Shandy." This appreciation for Sterne's literary style reflects lessing's unique perspective and critical engagement with themes such as fidelity and loyalty, which he explored in his own plays and writings.

As a key figure in German literature, Lessing is frequently mentioned in the context of cultural discourse, and he engaged in correspondence with other influential literary figures of his time. His interactions included discussions with individuals such as Sara Meyer and reflections on the translation efforts of works, including the “Empfindsame Reise.” Lessing's correspondence often included references to Sterne, highlighting his influence on literary classification and critique.

Lessing is also recognized by contemporaries, such as Bode, for his role in providing aid and influence in translation work. His literary critiques and discussions are noted for their depth, as he analyzed and appreciated Sterne's narratives and the intricate use of borrowed ideas within them. Furthermore, Lessing's legacy is characterized by his desire to see Sterne's literary heritage continue, underscoring his role as a thinker committed to the dialogues that shape literary interpretation and scholarship.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b1ddd79524e91ba84eecbc707c7a2b7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb9f823daea4acf22b2dce0ec0b834ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3dcaffe826a353c7b1a0eff516a2419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c3f247ede6e2e4cbb7778c1b56fd58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb3d3d51e372c48bb1c3585adf76c5fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc64252e1565a88b1d7729211672d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d15e55fa6a03a4ae9a73fae85bc97ec2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559b00cb6dc756396bfc420ba8cc5cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eb63434ade7863dbb529206940c54f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84307003973059440e3b98bafcdbef48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9514ef0c01ef6384fdf0e7549eeccb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4a45157e34604d157e56225b4b8622b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a99d58be4f096b2bbc3dd443af69754</data>
