    <node id="Allgemeine Deutsche Bibliothek">
      <data key="d0">Allgemeine Deutsche Bibliothek</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Allgemeine Deutsche Bibliothek is a prominent literary publication that serves as a comprehensive review platform for various literary works and authors. It is known for its critical insights into the narratives and stylistic features of significant texts, such as the Swiss translation of Laurence Sterne's sermons, which was praised for its narrative style. The publication not only evaluates the literary significance of Sterne's contributions but also discusses other important translations, including Bode's, expressing aspirations for further literary endeavors in the future.

In addition to its reviews, the Allgemeine Deutsche Bibliothek plays a critical role in literary discourse by addressing issues of authenticity in literary works. It has condemned certain actions by authors, as evidenced by its critique of Jacobi. Furthermore, it has been noted for its engagement with buzzwords and neologisms in the works of authors like Schummel, offering commentary on their use and implications within the literary landscape.

The organization is also recognized as a bibliographic resource that operated between 1765 and 1792, with its compilations originating from Berlin and Stettin. Throughout its history, the Allgemeine Deutsche Bibliothek has functioned as both a source of literary criticism and a cataloging reference, capturing various authors' influences and their reception by the broader literary community. Overall, it continues to be a significant reference point for discussions surrounding literary authenticity and critical reception in German literature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-939e417a7df4f7cc2019f7a0a8f2b15a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ebe193334de57430520a945aa53a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42cef61a79d34e5bcf885a966963554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f7d055c140a23788c7b5cad8fb7948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11d94df1514c9134e03d19c4744e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6830a00197a03b02eae670e7f2e9ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9514ef0c01ef6384fdf0e7549eeccb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9616c39c6806c71b17146575a3dbfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8429a197795773b69fd79fc5921e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-458f12b07f966802c9353e65d5abc548</data>
