      <data key="d2">Fielding is an English writer whose critiques and narratives provided a contrasting influence on German literature post-Richardson.&lt;SEP&gt;Fielding is referenced for his contributions to literature, emphasizing the absence of similar figures in German letters.&lt;SEP&gt;Fielding is a notable author in the company that welcomes Bode’s spirit in a poetic narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Fielding is another author mentioned in connection with Wezel's narrative style and specific story elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Fielding is an author whose influence is noted alongside Sterne in the context of literary imitation in works such as Tobias Knaut.&lt;SEP&gt;Fielding is a writer whose tavern and way-faring adventures share thematic similarities with themes found in Briefe Auf Einer Reise Aus Lothringen.</data>
