      <data key="d2">Zückert is the translator of the first six parts of "Tristram Shandy", published in 1763, noted for his interpretation of Sterne's work.&lt;SEP&gt;Zückert is mentioned as a translator whose work is criticized for inaccuracies in translating Sterne's text.&lt;SEP&gt;Zückert is mentioned as a predecessor to Bode, whose translation is criticized for being literal and inaccurate.&lt;SEP&gt;Zückert is associated with a translation mentioned in the text, indicating involvement in literature.</data>
