    <node id="Timme">
      <data key="d0">Timme</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Timme critiques misunderstood imitations of Yorick's work and discusses the literary impact of sentimentality.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is the author whose narrative style imitates Sterne’s method of satire in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is an author who employs satire in their narrative, repeating motifs while varying the conditions of the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is an author who wrote a satirical novel that received mixed reviews and was compared to Sterne's works.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is the author of a novel noted for its burlesque and satire, contrasting with the tone of Wezel’s writing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c22d20d40b43b3d2c1dbb21d56b7f2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fffe095b624cf5296e4dd35470f940d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef7a5904617eb5f54e94c5ea84fd0b1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95bd5a42403a89f556cf4ccd4b82fd6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4d01e530f294f930479d90da05382af</data>
