    <node id="German Literature">
      <data key="d0">German Literature</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">German literature is the subject of study regarding the influence of other literatures, particularly English.&lt;SEP&gt;German Literature is characterized by its perceived lack of humor and originality, as argued by various critics.&lt;SEP&gt;German Literature in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries was influenced by Sterne’s writing style and thematic exploration.&lt;SEP&gt;German Literature refers to the body of work influenced by Sterne, particularly in the context of sentimentalism and its opposition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-073c32eb7cfcec94cf8952d9901d1c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c7457182fd8c984b4b4d5b338a0a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5c550c793c251f99502adc3abd77fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757a7ae57a284fa20e40220b7c7af037</data>
