    <node id="Empfindsamkeit">
      <data key="d0">Empfindsamkeit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Empfindsamkeit is a literary movement that originated in Germany, characterized by its emphasis on sentimentality and emotional depth. This movement advocates for heightened sensitivity and introspection in emotional expression, often focusing on moral feelings such as joy or sorrow related to good and evil. It serves as a counterpoint to the literary styles of other authors, notably being referenced as a force opposed to Laurence Sterne's writing style.

Within German literature, Empfindsamkeit is noted for its prevalence and has been critiqued across various works, including those of notable critics such as Timme and Wezel. These critiques often highlight the movement's focus on sentimentality, questioning its excessive emotionalism and its influence on narrative structure. 

Moreover, Empfindsamkeit is defined as a movement that emphasizes the balance of emotional expression, allowing for a richer exploration of characters' internal states. This contrasts with another movement, Empfindelei, further delineating its unique stance within the broader landscape of literary movements centered around emotions and moral sensibility. Through its focus on character introspection and emotional sensitivity, Empfindsamkeit has left a significant mark on German literature, driving discussions on the role of sentimentality in narrative and moral expression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c22d20d40b43b3d2c1dbb21d56b7f2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fffe095b624cf5296e4dd35470f940d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30eda9443e1378b86c375a7fe5c0eb06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835b2b68b00b2bd674ad666036ecbc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20e923d9f373c003f6f48eba70750766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b979cdc44cde067d90763ef953998ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56a19306fc0bdd6d75f01267c814f30c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4d01e530f294f930479d90da05382af</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763621832</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Germany">
      <data key="d0">Germany</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Germany, as a nation, is recognized for its significant engagement with the literary works of Laurence Sterne, particularly in the context of the development and reception of his texts. The country experienced a notable popularity of Sterne's works, which inspired both appreciation and imitation among its literary circles. This cultural exchange showcases Germany's response to English literature, highlighting its influence on German literary traditions.

The literary conditions in Germany have also been subjects of critique, especially concerning the perceived lack of humor in its literature compared to that of English storytelling. This gap has been a focal point for discussions regarding how Sterne's literary style and humor were received in Germany, illustrating a complex relationship in literary appreciation and interpretation.

In particular, Sterne's "Sentimental Journey" found a resonance in Germany, aligning with the emotional experiences and literary aesthetics promoted by the sentimental movement, known in German as Empfindsamkeit. The conception of Yorick's character, a crucial figure in Sterne's narrative, flourished in this cultural environment, further demonstrating the depth of influence Sterne's works had on German literature. Overall, Germany is a key player in the discourse surrounding the reception, influence, and critique of Laurence Sterne's literary contributions.&lt;SEP&gt;Germany is mentioned as the origin of Rudolph, indicating his background.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c22d20d40b43b3d2c1dbb21d56b7f2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3445af39103910094e6f39b4e9d594d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b57f8b57daf11b165b8852ab7e62eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eb63434ade7863dbb529206940c54f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6830a00197a03b02eae670e7f2e9ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bed52ff145a82972c1126c22e4c660b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757a7ae57a284fa20e40220b7c7af037&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad7eb91ef19d9479c183ea94881f5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd506e2b4ab4403262e3cf611653609b</data>
