    <node id="Shandy">
      <data key="d0">Shandy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Shandy refers to Sterne's book, which is subject to translation and criticism in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Shandy refers to Sterne's earlier work "Tristram Shandy," which, although different in nature, is connected through its themes of sentiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Shandy is referenced as an author whose quotes are cited, indicating a humorous and critical literary style.&lt;SEP&gt;Shandy is referenced in discussions of literary works, noted with a page number and context.&lt;SEP&gt;Shandy is a reference to another of Sterne’s works that provides a model for Timme's narrative style and satirical approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Shandy is another work associated with Sterne that influences Timme's narrative.</data>
