    <node id="Herder">
      <data key="d0">Herder</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Herder critiques the German tendency for imitation in his works and later expresses a more positive view of it.&lt;SEP&gt;Herder is a representative of German literati and shows appreciation for Sterne's writings, particularly during his time in Riga.&lt;SEP&gt;Herder is a prominent figure in German literature, and his correspondence and works are explored in relation to cultural influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Herder is a literary figure known for his advocacy of Bode’s work and influence on the appreciation of Sterne.&lt;SEP&gt;Herder is mentioned as a mentor to Goethe, promoting the works of Sterne during their time in Strassburg.&lt;SEP&gt;Herder is a notable figure involved in correspondence with Joh. Heinrich Merck and other contemporaries.&lt;SEP&gt;Herder is another literary figure who expressed unequivocal appreciation for Sterne's work in a similar manner to Lessing and Goethe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-003097ce0b9615e69c58849744d9a337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5c550c793c251f99502adc3abd77fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eb63434ade7863dbb529206940c54f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9514ef0c01ef6384fdf0e7549eeccb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9616c39c6806c71b17146575a3dbfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c128264faa77a054077d4c6bfd355759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f99047222f973cdfa74a4aaa41bc1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
