      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Governor">
      <data key="d0">Governor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Governor refers to the official authority responsible for the administration of a colony or territory, such as Lord Gosford in Canada.&lt;SEP&gt;The Governor engages in conversation regarding anti-slavery subjects, displaying a dismissive attitude toward the abolition efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Governor is a Moorish official who interacted with the narrator during their leave from Mogador and imposed restrictions on European merchants.&lt;SEP&gt;The Governor is a character responsible for keeping the British Consul and his wife safe from the Moors during a bombardment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f63400d8188502b67eda00c561659eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd02a45e5de5d4ef105b2b38ed4ab33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c246ad7923d08e2ef2366af23b4c19f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763626560</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="English Canadians">
      <data key="d0">English Canadians</data>
      <data key="d1">group</data>
      <data key="d2">English Canadians refer to the English-speaking population in Canada who sought to maintain control over the political landscape during the period.&lt;SEP&gt;English Canadians refer to the group of English-speaking inhabitants in Canada, with concerns regarding governance and constitutional rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f63400d8188502b67eda00c561659eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b39e2cfb1e3f641af2dc7d617761e850</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622255</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="French Canadians">
      <data key="d0">French Canadians</data>
      <data key="d1">group</data>
      <data key="d2">French Canadians refer to the French-speaking population in Canada who were engaged in political and social struggles against English dominance.&lt;SEP&gt;French Canadians refers to the inhabitants of Canada of French descent, who had complex loyalties during historical conflicts.&lt;SEP&gt;French Canadians are a group that perceived a bill as a threat to their national existence and took action against it.&lt;SEP&gt;French Canadians are the group of people in Canada whose rights and language were advocated for by politicians like Lord Gosford and Papineau.&lt;SEP&gt;French Canadians are a cultural group in Canada who sought to assert their rights and governance during the political tensions highlighted in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;French Canadians are referred to collectively as a group involved in various movements and conflicts during this period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f63400d8188502b67eda00c561659eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac7fb6c5e874c886dbb8df30d7d6fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b39e2cfb1e3f641af2dc7d617761e850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353f63fa013a00ee4a62ffebc8c022a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da749e17a56c35554061ac541d67d08c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b195a27b43ec85da2d0175fa01cef0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41f4557b5a58dc496c18ce0c8f8f2c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392528a8e340519b1401fbf1b71aad8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622255</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
