    <node id="Wolfred Nelson">
      <data key="d0">Wolfred Nelson</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Wolfred Nelson is an English-speaking politician and a prominent leader within the Patriotes movement during the 1837-1838 rebellions in Canada. He was a close associate of Louis-Joseph Papineau, providing strategic advice particularly during the engagement at St. Denis. Notably, Wolfred Nelson advocated for armed resistance and readiness, urging fellow insurgents to prepare for conflict as tensions escalated before the rebellion.

Despite facing significant challenges, including capture by loyalist militia, Wolfred Nelson played a crucial role in rallying support for the Patriotes. His leadership contributed to a notable victory at St. Denis, which inspired further insurgent activity in places like St. Eustache. Nelson's involvement in the movement is underscored by his relationship as the brother of Robert Nelson, another key figure in the struggle for independence, and he is referenced alongside him concerning the independence proclamation.

After the rebellions, Wolfred Nelson was one of the notable political prisoners whose situation was less severe than others who were executed. He eventually returned to Montreal and re-entered political life, being elected to parliament, signifying his enduring impact on the political landscape following the turmoil of the rebellion. His dual role as a medical professional and political figure further highlights the diverse contributions he made during this pivotal period in Canadian history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d3c806038738c5cf824708ed3cfff5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0099aaf0d6a5d5b602247be491e3fb1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349529243dbc83f8fcf9f0443bec18f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb71f32b0ab08e17e4d6cb83be9c380c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6059f7b6685e9fbba6db55d93c65ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92528df8108a5a90a2c2b6e9d79fa6a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26bd7dcdcc38c1ce5338b530f0ab8694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d67b8f87397b56d105fc32a0b1f677&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc668a337064f7982e9ba35184cf528</data>
