      <data key="d2">Lord Durham is a political figure who left Quebec in 1838 and is noted for his report on colonial affairs in British North America.&lt;SEP&gt;Lord Durham is a historical figure whose amnesty encouraged some inhabitants to believe that rebellion was a minor offense.&lt;SEP&gt;Lord Durham wrote a report analyzing the situation that led to the Lower Canada Rebellion.&lt;SEP&gt;Lord Durham is associated with political decisions affecting Canada, particularly in relation to the amnesty.</data>
