      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Upper Canada is one of the two provinces into which Canada was divided in 1791, predominantly English-speaking.&lt;SEP&gt;Upper Canada was a historical region primarily English-speaking, created following the division of Canada in 1791.&lt;SEP&gt;Upper Canada is mentioned as a region proposed for legislative union with Lower Canada.</data>
