    <node id="Minnesota">
      <data key="d0">Minnesota</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Minnesota is the U.S. state noted for its significant historical and political events during the 19th century, particularly in the year 1859, which included various elections and a notable lynching incident. This period was marked by heightened tensions and unrest, reflective of the broader conflicts occurring across the nation as the Civil War approached.

Admitted to the Union during the Civil War, Minnesota was impacted by the tumultuous atmosphere of the time. Local news reporting reflected the regional dynamics, which were heavily influenced by the ongoing national conflict. The state was also a focal point for significant violence and strife as historical events unfolded, including incidents described in the context of civil unrest.

Minnesota has a profound Native American history characterized by land disputes and conflicts, particularly during the Civil War. The state witnessed significant events such as the Indian War and the subsequent military tribunal, highlighting its role in these transformative events. 

In addition to its military and political significance, Minnesota was the site where the first session of the territorial legislature convened in a hotel building, demonstrating the early organizational efforts in governance. Capt. Acker, who served in a prominent military position as adjutant general, also played a role in resonating national issues within Minnesota.

Agriculturally, Minnesota experienced a remarkable transformation, shown by a nearly 100% increase in the number of farms during this period. This growth indicates the state's evolving economic landscape and its adaptation to the changing social and political climate of the time. Through these various events, Minnesota has carved a distinctive and important place in American history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5b84432ad1a7600b31aab3ee4243129&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2440d11a9db0e7c5ec428e134dc47e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7096033ca5d17f317a3de07c28f9b0bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b75c5f4f7c0385a783e34fd555b4a0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46289654522dd0ee1ffdeb77be06722d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-259cd15d2a822dcb52e2f16a8974a319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d6821bdddaee230e47cab021a16e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71098a84f862320370cd4b30b1083858</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624064</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Geo. W. Moore">
      <data key="d0">Geo. W. Moore</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
