    <node id="Pioneer">
      <data key="d0">Pioneer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Pioneer is a newspaper that published both genuine and bogus news during the time of the described events.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer is a newspaper that competed for the timeliness of publishing the president's message during a significant news event.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer was the first publication issued from the Empire saloon's printing office on April 10, 1849.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer is noted as the first paper printed in St. Paul, Minnesota.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer was a newspaper where several noted printers worked and served in various capacities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer is a newspaper where Marshall Robinson worked and where Earle S. Goodrich was the editor-in-chief.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-253bf03f6503d8e5da2098445ef9b630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a4789d4f1f7c874d43ac8b35b4ece9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49b770a2f437d2a1478f52b0f2747ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbf9f440f0bef7a0809b533af91c73a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20726b17616075ddbd2a847a83ea89f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be8b49c919bf06f613da48187833e98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ddaddeaf94d2bcd3da95a9c4f85c42</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
