    <node id="Fire Department">
      <data key="d0">Fire Department</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fire Department worked hard to combat the fire at the hotel, even without immediate access to water supplies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fire Department in St. Paul was responsible for responding to fires, including the destructive event on March 16, 1860.&lt;SEP&gt;The St. Paul fire department participated in the procession and celebrations for Washington's Birthday.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bf33d450055327352cd4545502529ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbf9f440f0bef7a0809b533af91c73a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf8943ee8dd238feb8fd1d1ea67c1d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d26c30cc3102d9679f3880d6b7c95b61</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Snow-Covered Streets">
      <data key="d0">Snow-Covered Streets</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Snow-Covered Streets refer to the streets where guests escaped onto after the fire, often without adequate clothing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bf33d450055327352cd4545502529ee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Furniture">
      <data key="d0">Furniture</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Furniture included costly pianos and upholstered items that were thrown into the street during the fire evacuation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bf33d450055327352cd4545502529ee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Expensive Articles">
      <data key="d0">Expensive Articles</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Expensive Articles refer to valuable items that were dropped in the snow during the panic and evacuation from the hotel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bf33d450055327352cd4545502529ee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Col. AC Jones">
      <data key="d0">Col. AC Jones</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Col. AC Jones is the adjutant general of the state and served as the marshal-in-chief of the parade.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d26c30cc3102d9679f3880d6b7c95b61</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pioneer Guards">
      <data key="d0">Pioneer Guards</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Pioneer Guards was a military company called upon by Governor Sibley to respond to the lynching incident.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer Guards are the oldest military company in the state, featured prominently in the parade, and received new rifles and bayonets.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer Guards was a group that participated in celebrations and social events in St. Paul and disbanded after the war began.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pioneer Guards was a military company formed by Capt. Acker, known for its quality at that time in the West.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d26c30cc3102d9679f3880d6b7c95b61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46289654522dd0ee1ffdeb77be06722d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-259cd15d2a822dcb52e2f16a8974a319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf8943ee8dd238feb8fd1d1ea67c1d4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="City Guards">
      <data key="d0">City Guards</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The City Guards, led by Capt. John O'Gorman, participated in the parade following the Pioneer Guards.&lt;SEP&gt;The City Guards was an organization that participated in the procession during Washington's Birthday celebrations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d26c30cc3102d9679f3880d6b7c95b61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf8943ee8dd238feb8fd1d1ea67c1d4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763622770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
