    <node id="Achilles">
      <data key="d0">Achilles</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Achilles is a famous warrior in Greek mythology, noted for being inflamed by Briseis and his participation in the Trojan War.&lt;SEP&gt;Achilles is a legendary Greek hero known for his prowess in battle, mentioned in relation to themes of valor and bravery.&lt;SEP&gt;Achilles is a figure from Greek mythology known for his role in the Trojan War and his mother Thetis, who was a goddess of the sea.&lt;SEP&gt;Achilles is referenced as a heroic figure whose story is suggested to be a potential subject for poetry.&lt;SEP&gt;Achilles is referenced as another figure associated with grief due to death, paralleling the themes of loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Achilles is a renowned Greek hero in mythology known for his role in the Trojan War and his iconic shield.&lt;SEP&gt;Achilles is known in mythology for his spear and his connection to the healing of Telephus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a8a704560f9aa2b54ceb8b9a6fd26a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba3706ec176b6f1bdc3b92e3affac80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af75b0ed4f2d647b015eaa8b0eac561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f54377361394a10337ee324609f05a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b39f09bb068668fc5d13770de07db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49e205c56dbae8d49f65c119fc9144a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763623213</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hector">
      <data key="d0">Hector</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hector is a Trojan prince and warrior, described as going into battle after embracing his wife, Andromache.&lt;SEP&gt;Hector is depicted as a tragic hero, whose actions and fate are mentioned in connection with themes of loss and valor in warfare.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a8a704560f9aa2b54ceb8b9a6fd26a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af75b0ed4f2d647b015eaa8b0eac561</data>
