    <node id="Hippolytus">
      <data key="d0">Hippolytus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hippolytus is referenced in the context of love and desire, suggesting his significance in romantic pursuits.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippolytus is referenced as a character whose qualities could invoke desire, compared to the powerful figure of Priapus.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippolytus is mentioned as part of a narrative surrounding themes of tragedy and unrequited love.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippolytus is mentioned as an example of chastity in the context of contrasting characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippolytus is a figure from mythology referenced for the dangers faced by charioteers when racing.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippolytus is a mythological character associated with Phaedra, mentioned in the context of letter exchanges.</data>
