    <node id="Wine">
      <data key="d0">Wine</data>
      <data key="d1">product</data>
      <data key="d2">The wine is highlighted as a drink that plays a significant role in the romantic entreaties and interactions described in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is a natural substance mentioned as part of a scene that contributes to revealing hidden truths in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine was the principal beverage for Roman slaves, consumed occasionally and allowed in small amounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is described in the context of social gatherings and its presentation on the table after a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is an alcoholic beverage made from the fermentation of grape-juice.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is a fermented beverage made from grape-juice, containing alcohol and flavor from the grapes, and can affect the consumer's behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is an alcoholic beverage produced by fermenting grapes, which may contain less alcohol than distilled liquors.</data>
