      <data key="d0">Bacchus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Bacchus is referenced as a figure associated with wine and revelry, representing indulgence and fearlessness in love.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacchus symbolizes joy and triumph and is mentioned in the context of overcoming challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacchus is a Roman god associated with wine and revelry, mentioned as being without fear.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacchus is another deity mentioned in relation to beauty and the desirability of hair.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacchus is the god of wine and revelry, acknowledged for his youthful and joyous nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacchus is identified as the Roman god of wine, associated with triumphs that extend to the river Ganges in Ovid's context.</data>
