    <node id="Venus">
      <data key="d0">Venus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Venus is the Roman goddess of love, known for her strong associations with themes of romance, beauty, and relationships. She is portrayed as a divine figure whose influence transcends mere passion; rather, she symbolizes fidelity and affection in love. In various narratives, she stands as a recipient of dedications, often linked to the act of offering tablets in her name, signifying her importance in personal aspirations and worship.

As the goddess of love, Venus is depicted in contexts that highlight her maternal aspects, especially in relation to her son Tibullus, where she illustrates profound maternal sorrow after his death. This highlights a complex layer to her character, portraying her not only as an emblem of romantic love but also as a figure embodying deep emotional connections within familial relations. Additionally, she is invoked in oaths and pledges concerning fidelity and is often compared to other divine figures, including her connections to Cupid and Mars, further enriching her narrative presence.

Culturally, Venus is also likened to an astrological entity, referred to as a rising star that brings good fortune. Her imagery varies widely across artistic interpretations; one notable depiction includes her emerging from the sea in a famous painting by Apelles. Venus is specifically revered in Amathus, a city in Cyprus, illustrating local worship practices and the geographical significance of her cult.

Through these multifaceted representations, Venus emerges as a potent symbol of love and beauty, celebrated in literature, mythology, and the arts, while her various associations with joy, passion, and maternal care illustrate her enduring impact on human emotions and relationships.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a8a704560f9aa2b54ceb8b9a6fd26a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91ae32cc554dc390c60bd5c873778659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a40ad400e6c46c8451bc02d5c90eeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d9981c359a23239322d1ef69f6eabb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e60239d7bab05fbce9d289bd08db986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d5602a32bc951267c6f93a5e9e14aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f54377361394a10337ee324609f05a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba43616fff0b8112616e172e23cfa8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb2899f1a356a92ddd5741e19e4f7f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1c921bbb2e03c67dfc84088fb4c60fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff2030ce7e35257099d54aca8256ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a58ce86fabb001a8e0add34c5408f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4958bc3b034dd7b59c1c0df2fab2b8d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49e205c56dbae8d49f65c119fc9144a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094a55bf6bce40e6d7aa0cbb6247afe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9d540a7609b6ba4c69dd1651e5329e</data>
