    <node id="Jupiter">
      <data key="d0">Jupiter</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Jupiter is referred to as a powerful figure and deity, reflecting themes of strength and authority in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Jupiter is a deity who hurls fire at groves and towers but forbids striking a perjured woman.&lt;SEP&gt;Jupiter is mentioned in relation to the concept of wealth and seduction, symbolizing power and influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Jupiter is the Roman god mentioned for transforming into various forms, representing divinity and power.&lt;SEP&gt;Jupiter is the Roman god referred to in the context of myths related to other figures and events.&lt;SEP&gt;Jupiter is depicted as having offered violence to Ceres and is associated with Cybele as her husband.&lt;SEP&gt;Jupiter is a major god in mythology, often associated with thunder and punishment of giants like Tityus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64676dc63a3bd3d7dc906d1feffc619e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1af75b0ed4f2d647b015eaa8b0eac561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24655aa74002f9c9a1716299b6bb40bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714b6c3790dfcbb71e477248f2e13f46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4315ba5dfb6f6d19c3b64e08d29cdc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-442f3a60382a33a67c2d1a47639643cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ae1d708e454e0e6bf3e72d6ca49fad</data>
