    <node id="Ceres">
      <data key="d0">Ceres</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ceres is the goddess of agriculture and fertility, honored by husbandmen within the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceres is mentioned regarding her seed that brought growth and fertility to uncultivated ground, symbolizing nourishment and agricultural abundance.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceres is a goddess associated with agriculture and fertility, who oversees the rites that cause separation between lovers and influences crop growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceres is the Roman goddess of agriculture, who is linked to the myth of Triptolemus and the introduction of farming.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceres is the goddess associated with a festival noted for specific rituals and customs in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceres is characterized by her chastity and the subject of accusations from Ovid regarding her relationship with Jupiter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64676dc63a3bd3d7dc906d1feffc619e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c9855ea8a01287d6710833c29e4d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29eddb27a800eedb331c3ac515bfc570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4315ba5dfb6f6d19c3b64e08d29cdc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1c921bbb2e03c67dfc84088fb4c60fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ae80ee2d9a869de6cf9860587e59e14</data>
