    <node id="Sulmo">
      <data key="d0">Sulmo</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Sulmo is a small town in Italy, specifically in the region of Pelignian land, mentioned in the context of the speaker's locale.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo is a location described as a small but pleasant area in Pelignian land, known for its flowing streams.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo is referenced as a place with walls and is significant in the context of the speaker's origins.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo is a town of the Peligni and is noted as the birthplace of a poet mentioned in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo is a location referenced in relation to the journey from Rome and associated with Corinna's travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo is a town near which a river flows, significant for its historical and geographical context in relation to Ovid.</data>
