    <node id="Ilia">
      <data key="d0">Ilia</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ilia is a mythical figure who is associated with the founding of Rome and the mother of Romulus and Remus.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilia is depicted as a descendant of Laomedon, wandering alone in sorrow and experiencing emotional turmoil.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilia is referenced as the mother of Romulus and Remus, important figures in Roman mythology, symbolizing lineage and heritage.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilia is a character associated with various myths concerning her burial and marriage to a river.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cf5cee73398d032581450496a09223dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03db9ea051409884799c6fabae5a4d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f54377361394a10337ee324609f05a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ae80ee2d9a869de6cf9860587e59e14</data>
