    <node id="Noah">
      <data key="d0">Noah</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Noah is referenced as the Poet who addresses themes of love and the immortal fame of poets in his elegies.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah is a character reflecting on love, beauty, and the complex feelings associated with relationships and fidelity.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah is a constable who interacts with Georgiana and Sir Tristram regarding the missing Dean.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah is a constable who took a man in the Deanery Stables and is involved in leading him to Durnstone.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah is mentioned as having made decisions that led to his brother's misfortune, including taking Kitty in a cart.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah is a character who expresses his frustrations regarding his wife and confronts the Dean about personal matters.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah is a character present in the log who experiences various daily activities and interactions with family and friends.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03db9ea051409884799c6fabae5a4d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c781927a13f05b8bf3cc68dedd0ed839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba43616fff0b8112616e172e23cfa8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51763246a424f17d012c8a8c92b9dd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59edcbf702bf09e6c7842114ee9fee90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e596e9ce7637f90613b8207baadae53e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe1560cf60e9d4a7338b3d121ff45e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1005fe668029a3498fae762b9e2347d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2923fc0c238f18810f053d6e390e261d</data>
