    <node id="Penelope">
      <data key="d0">Penelope</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Penelope is a character mentioned in the text as having tested the strength of young men using her bow.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is a character stressing the importance of entertaining lovers and making strategic choices in love and presentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is noted for remaining undefiled despite the presence of many suitors.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is the wife of Ulysses in mythology, known for her loyalty and patience as she awaits his return.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714b6c3790dfcbb71e477248f2e13f46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba43616fff0b8112616e172e23cfa8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ab58d75e0d33f2fb45c933ce510e99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49e205c56dbae8d49f65c119fc9144a</data>
