      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Apollo is referenced as a deity who might covet the beauty of another's hair.&lt;SEP&gt;Apollo is referenced as a God wielding a flexible bow.&lt;SEP&gt;Apollo is mentioned as a deity represented by a statue on the Palatine Hill, linked to poetry and riches.&lt;SEP&gt;Apollo is a significant figure in mythology, known as the god of music, arts, and the father of Orpheus.&lt;SEP&gt;Apollo is a major god in mythology who inflicted punishment on Tityus.</data>
