    <node id="Tibullus">
      <data key="d0">Tibullus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Tibullus is a poet who is mourned in the text, passionate about his love and his connection with the goddess Ceres.&lt;SEP&gt;Tibullus is the poet lamented in Elegy IX, noted for his death and significance in poetic lore.&lt;SEP&gt;Tibullus is a Roman poet who was an intimate friend of Æmilius Macer and is mentioned in conjunction with Ovid and Virgil.&lt;SEP&gt;Tibullus is a poet who alludes to various cultural and mythical themes in his writings, including references to individuals like Delia and Isis.&lt;SEP&gt;Tibullus is a Roman poet referenced multiple times in discussing themes of love and mourning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c9d540a7609b6ba4c69dd1651e5329e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29eddb27a800eedb331c3ac515bfc570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4315ba5dfb6f6d19c3b64e08d29cdc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ab58d75e0d33f2fb45c933ce510e99</data>
