      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Corcyra, now known as Corfu, is referenced as the ancient land of the Phæacians, with historical significance in Tibullus's life and writing.&lt;SEP&gt;Corcyra is mentioned in contrast to Rome, serving a significant contextual purpose in the text.</data>
