      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tragedy is another poetic form, characterized by intense emotions and dramatic themes, which the Poet contemplates as an alternative to writing Elegies.&lt;SEP&gt;Tragedy is a dramatic genre that Ovid suggests has connections to the Elegiac measure and Greek influences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64ce64b0a51b17a08eb9a938fb755d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc0c02df8cb82b091fb73a066662a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa28345d39e77952274cbff7d1c3944e</data>
