      <data key="d0">Padre</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Padre is a preacher who speaks earnestly to the audience, engaging them with honesty and a powerful voice.&lt;SEP&gt;The Padre is described as a tall patriarch who listens to Rudolph's narrative and offers subtle feedback.&lt;SEP&gt;The Padre is depicted as a tall, ungainly patriarch who listens shrewdly to narratives and appears to hold authority in the setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The padre in the council is characterized as one who is present during the discussions but knowledgeable about local conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The padre is a character who reads a message and offers insights concerning it, using a cigar.&lt;SEP&gt;The padre is a character who is responsible for the welfare of a wounded convert and provides directions to the group.&lt;SEP&gt;The padre is a character with excessive zeal for saving souls, who mistakenly tries to lasso a devil instead of a young girl.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-409131abbfafd74396f07aa2c2df7b16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb115037ebf479e3fa9826264e2a73f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f06afe6acd299e703bd0c0fadd159c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8decdd14fcac24539dbd5c797ec474&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe3a458e44f6e2041ed190afdf2aa9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7efad2dc71a14d371ba2b2fc8d92a271&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a98afa31aca72fe4aab8a13ac827087</data>
