    <node id="The House">
      <data key="d0">The House</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The House is the setting where critical interactions and emotional turmoil occur between the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;The House is the location that is burning, creating chaos and noise in the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The House is described as tightly closed, creating a sense of foreboding and mystery within the scene.&lt;SEP&gt;The House is associated with Miss Flora and is described as being in a concealed location that poses dangers.&lt;SEP&gt;The house is the physical space that is currently under the control of the law, impacting Cissy's living situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The house belongs to Miss Trixit's father, which is currently under Jake Poole's possession due to legal circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;The house is described as dark and gloomy, resembling the doctor and serving as the setting for Eileen's captivity.</data>
