    <node id="Polaris">
      <data key="d0">Polaris</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Polaris is a star used for navigation, often referred to as the North Star, and is essential for determining azimuth and latitude.&lt;SEP&gt;Polaris is the North Star, pivotal in navigation and observation for finding the meridian.&lt;SEP&gt;Polaris, also known as Ursae Minoris, is a bright circumpolar star used in navigation, specifically for determining the true meridian.&lt;SEP&gt;Polaris is a star utilized for celestial navigation, specifically noted for its position during observations.&lt;SEP&gt;Polaris is a star used in celestial navigation to determine altitude and is pointed to during observations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-542ef42b55daca6f5424b791e6bd2765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee9c14e4874d5edaebe46bb34bc7c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7ddc2e019049a9912f840df02ad08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1573d79bcfed29e4fb110ec5c56a26fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38361c9228288e8fce93f69ba0277336</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624046</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sextant">
      <data key="d0">Sextant</data>
      <data key="d1">instrument</data>
      <data key="d2">A sextant is a navigation instrument used to measure the angle between an astronomical object and the horizon for determining latitude.&lt;SEP&gt;A sextant is a navigation instrument used to measure angular distances between objects, particularly in celestial navigation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-542ef42b55daca6f5424b791e6bd2765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7ddc2e019049a9912f840df02ad08a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624046</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Horizon">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Horizon</data>
      <data key="d1">instrument</data>
      <data key="d2">An artificial horizon is a device used in conjunction with a sextant to establish a horizontal reference for measuring angles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-542ef42b55daca6f5424b791e6bd2765</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624046</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Zenith Distance">
      <data key="d0">Zenith Distance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Zenith distance refers to the angle between a celestial object and the zenith, used in calculating altitude.</data>
