      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Western elongation refers to the position of Polaris when it is observed moving downward in relation to the observer's meridian.&lt;SEP&gt;Western elongation refers to the position of a celestial body when it is setting in the west, significant for timing observations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-542ef42b55daca6f5424b791e6bd2765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38361c9228288e8fce93f69ba0277336</data>
