    <node id="Ocellated Pheasant">
      <data key="d0">Ocellated Pheasant</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The Ocellated Pheasant is mentioned in the section of Natural History within the Scientific American Supplement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ocellated Pheasant, scientifically known as _Rheinardius ocellatus_, is a bird characterized by its distinctive tail feathers and beak, which has unique features compared to other gallinaceans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ocellated Pheasant is a species of bird recently presented as a specimen with unique characteristics, contributing to the understanding of Phasianidae.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e8c3f67ad6c5ab11a1aa1c43bc0fc53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ab7ad03b323561e72dda983ec2d3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2beb62a30fe2b1c57e576db27e8e584f</data>
