      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">New York is a state that includes marble buildings such as the old City Hall and the Custom House in New York City.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is referenced as a destination the police plan to take the arrested individual.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is the destination mentioned in the context of transporting Arlie Lane after his arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is the city where Latimer conducts his work and where his interactions with the Bishop take place.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is referred to as an "unclean, wicked city" and is contrasted with rural life by the Old Man.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is the location where Miss Catherwaight seeks and collects her medals from pawnshops.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is the city where Henry Burgoyne and Mr. Lockwood moved to continue their legal studies.</data>
