      <data key="d2">Granite is mentioned as a building stone with various sources in the architecture section.&lt;SEP&gt;Granite is a hard rock abundant in New England and was significantly used for construction and monumental purposes, particularly the variety from Quincy.&lt;SEP&gt;Granite is a durable stone used in construction, characterized by its ability to be cut into various shapes and sizes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a09a3405b807f7a33064172d2e463326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ab7ad03b323561e72dda983ec2d3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59ad55bacf8e991f7ec32f1bd324e6cb</data>
