      <data key="d2">Water is essential for nutrition and is a substance that can be included within the broader definition of food.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is a colorless and tasteless liquid essential for life, which differs significantly from alcohol in its properties, particularly in combustion.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is essential for the body, used in food preparation and is a major component of bodily structure; it must be clean to avoid illness.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is referenced in various traditions as being connected to the origins of musical instruments in myths across cultures.</data>
