    <node id="Azimuth">
      <data key="d0">Azimuth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Azimuth is the angle between a reference direction and a point in the sky, often calculated in astronomy for locating celestial objects.&lt;SEP&gt;Azimuth is a measurement in degrees used to denote the direction of an object from a specific point, particularly in astronomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Azimuth is the angle between the vertical plane of an object and the meridian plane, critical for determining celestial object positions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac7ddc2e019049a9912f840df02ad08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1573d79bcfed29e4fb110ec5c56a26fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38361c9228288e8fce93f69ba0277336</data>
