    <node id="S. S. Simon">
      <data key="d0">S. S. Simon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">S. S. Simon is the proprietor of a wood yard who is perceived to side with Brindle Bill, known for being a strong character in the community.&lt;SEP&gt;S. S. Simon is a character who acts as Brindle Bill's second during the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;S. S. Simon is a character involved in a conversation about family connections and financial matters in Shirt-Tail Bend.&lt;SEP&gt;S. S. Simon is a character involved in managing a business and dealing with financial transactions, including a significant amount of money.&lt;SEP&gt;S. S. Simon is referenced as the father of Young Simon, who is noted for his large estate.&lt;SEP&gt;S. S. Simon is Young Simon's father, a hard master and financier, who struggled with wealth and died from swamp fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rose Simon">
      <data key="d0">Rose Simon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Rose Simon is the wife of S. S. Simon, who receives news about her family's history and treasures from her keepsake box.&lt;SEP&gt;Rose Simon is the wife of S. S. Simon and the daughter of Tom Fairfield and Susan Lasco. She has a tragic outcome due to yellow fever.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tom Fairfield">
      <data key="d0">Tom Fairfield</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Tom Fairfield is a young man from Kentucky who aspires to improve his fortune and position, eventually considering becoming a preacher.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom Fairfield is a character descended from a prominent Virginia family with a restless spirit who moved to Kentucky as a boy.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom Fairfield is a character who sought to improve his fortune and faced several personal tragedies and misfortunes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom Fairfield is the father of Roxie and Suza, depicted as a drunkard who is presumed dead and has desert his children.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom Fairfield is a character whose presumed death prompts a significant reaction from the community, with neighbors attesting to his character.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom Fairfield is identified as the father of Rose Simon, as mentioned in a conversation about her family history.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom Fairfield is the father of Rose Simon and was previously married to Susan Lasco, with whom he has a child.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08b9d6f937baa20d8292bac71db403dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ac45ec6721641ae16ac8fcb28ed74f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416151ab22ab2af93343eed774c95e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab396e5290a1af8b37332288d9ad1b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c437983d26451567a1e6bf0d1cd6f13e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Susan Lasco">
      <data key="d0">Susan Lasco</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Susan Lasco is the mother of Rose Simon, whose name comes up in the context of family connections and inheritance.&lt;SEP&gt;Susan Lasco is the sister of John A. Lasco, missing for many years, and is the subject of her brother's quest and final wishes.&lt;SEP&gt;Susan Lasco is the mother of Rose Simon and was married to Tom Fairfield.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d6ba5697f9f6ac8decb2198a361839d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brindle Bill">
      <data key="d0">Brindle Bill</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Brindle Bill is a wood-chopper known for his strength and as a leading spirit in social gatherings, particularly at 'headquarters.'&lt;SEP&gt;Brindle Bill is portrayed as the stout man ready to fight Don Carlo, who claims insult and demands fair play.&lt;SEP&gt;Brindle Bill is a character with a hidden agenda, discussing family legacies and financial opportunities.&lt;SEP&gt;Brindle Bill is a character who engages in a financial agreement with S. S. Simon and is mentioned as being involved in some questionable activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d6ba5697f9f6ac8decb2198a361839d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sundown Hill">
      <data key="d0">Sundown Hill</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sundown Hill is a character who stands by Don Carlo during the confrontation against Brindle Bill.&lt;SEP&gt;Sundown Hill is mentioned as the location of a cabin where significant conversations occur among wood cutters after John A. Lasco's death.&lt;SEP&gt;Sundown Hill is mentioned as a character who testified regarding Rose Simon's parentage and was involved in a financial transaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Sundown Hill is a location referenced as the home of Steve Brindle's mother, impacting his family narrative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d6ba5697f9f6ac8decb2198a361839d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58817a44207e082297ea3faa165db2bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Port William">
      <data key="d0">Port William</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Port William is the name of the first settlement made at the mouth of the Kentucky River.&lt;SEP&gt;Port William is the location in Kentucky where Rose Simon and her sisters were separated.&lt;SEP&gt;Port William is a village where Aunt Katy resides and conducts her knitting business.&lt;SEP&gt;Port William is the setting for the events involving S. S. Simon, Rose Simon, and other characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Port William is the destination Suza Fairfield is trying to reach, where she hopes to find safety away from Aunt Katy.&lt;SEP&gt;Port William is the town where events unfold, including a camp meeting attended by Don Carlo.&lt;SEP&gt;Port William is described as the home and community of Suza Fairfield.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-308dc1f4e23e0e8a33feabd4ae43b18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80c6d1a10302d97782b2bc50d63133d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab396e5290a1af8b37332288d9ad1b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e347c91e271c6caaede3cd9a43e87b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shirt-Tail Bend">
      <data key="d0">Shirt-Tail Bend</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Shirt-Tail Bend is a locality characterized by wood-cutters and is known by boatmen for its connection to the wood yard established by Don and Dan Carlo.&lt;SEP&gt;Shirt-Tail Bend is a locality noted for its wood-cutting and absence of community improvements like schools or churches.&lt;SEP&gt;Shirt-Tail Bend is a rural location where important discussions and events about family and finances occur among the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Shirt-Tail Bend is the place to which S. S. Simon and party returned after a financial transaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Shirt-Tail Bend is a location associated with Don Carlo's character story.&lt;SEP&gt;Shirt-Tail Bend is a location referenced as the former residence of Steve Brindle's father.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58817a44207e082297ea3faa165db2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9445e78fa0e5990fbfc82fd7af0897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624316</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Belle of Port William">
      <data key="d0">The Belle of Port William</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Belle of Port William refers to a character archetype representing beauty and youth within the context of the story.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624317</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Aunt Katy">
      <data key="d0">Aunt Katy</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Aunt Katy is a relative who resides in a nearby cabin and is concerned for Roxie and her siblings.&lt;SEP&gt;Aunt Katy is a character depicted as a benefactress who comforts the little sisters and makes decisions regarding their care.&lt;SEP&gt;Aunt Katy is a central character known for her industriousness, financial independence, and her ambiguous will regarding her estate.&lt;SEP&gt;Aunt Katy is an old woman who is portrayed as the captor of Suza Fairfield, characterized by her oppressive presence and is described as sleeping when Suza returns.&lt;SEP&gt;Aunt Katy is a character who had money earned by her own hands and is related to the Demitt estate, inheriting a life interest.&lt;SEP&gt;Aunt Katy is a character who has secrets about her financial possessions and expresses a deep love for her foster child, Suza Fairfield.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08b9d6f937baa20d8292bac71db403dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-308dc1f4e23e0e8a33feabd4ae43b18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ac45ec6721641ae16ac8fcb28ed74f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80c6d1a10302d97782b2bc50d63133d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e347c91e271c6caaede3cd9a43e87b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624317</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Demitt Estate">
      <data key="d0">Demitt Estate</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Demitt Estate is an inherited property managed by various administrators after the passing of Old Demitt.&lt;SEP&gt;The Demitt estate is the property associated with the family of Old Demitt, which has passed through various administrators.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-308dc1f4e23e0e8a33feabd4ae43b18c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624317</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Old Demitt">
      <data key="d0">Old Demitt</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Old Demitt is a deceased character who passed away intestate, leading to complications regarding the estate's inheritance.&lt;SEP&gt;Old Demitt is a character who died intestate, resulting in the inheritance of his estate by relatives except for Aunt Katy's life interest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-308dc1f4e23e0e8a33feabd4ae43b18c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624317</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brother Demitt">
      <data key="d0">Brother Demitt</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Brother Demitt is a character who owned large tracts of land and slaves, playing a prominent role in the local society.&lt;SEP&gt;Brother Demitt is a character who presides over a council of settlers discussing the fate of the children of Tom Fairfield.&lt;SEP&gt;Brother Demitt is a character living in a double cabin made of hewn logs, observed by an observer during a significant moment in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Brother Demitt is a character who left Port William one cold evening, leading to a tragic outcome due to his intoxication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08b9d6f937baa20d8292bac71db403dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ac45ec6721641ae16ac8fcb28ed74f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab396e5290a1af8b37332288d9ad1b47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624317</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Young Simon">
      <data key="d0">Young Simon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Young Simon is the only son of S. S. Simon, noted for inheriting a large estate.&lt;SEP&gt;Young Simon is a cotton planter with four plantations and over six hundred slaves, struggling with the desire to become wealthy and lacking knowledge of his family history.&lt;SEP&gt;Young Simon is a character who suffers from consumption and is advised to take a trip to the West Indies for his health; he expresses interest in Roxie Daymon.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668c616fe700fcefe866c088d1613f74</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624318</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Roxie Daymon">
      <data key="d0">Roxie Daymon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Roxie Daymon, also known as Roxie Fairfield, is a historical figure associated with Young Simon's family's history.&lt;SEP&gt;Roxie Daymon is an interesting young lady from Chicago who is part of a pleasure trip to New Orleans and is described as beautiful but lacking family history.&lt;SEP&gt;Roxie Daymon is a character whose death is mentioned, and her legacy is discussed regarding her daughter and historical context.&lt;SEP&gt;Roxie Daymon is a young and beautiful woman who consents to marry Simon, who is dying.&lt;SEP&gt;Roxie Daymon is mentioned as a near relative involved in the case related to the Simon estate.&lt;SEP&gt;Roxie Daymon is a woman in Chicago who is viewed as rich and legally involved with the Simon estate during the war.&lt;SEP&gt;Roxie Daymon is described as a woman who married a young mechanic and found happiness in a cottage home.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b703ad46fc561ded805fade2af40be0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668c616fe700fcefe866c088d1613f74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1788abe5b20f786a0ee4558b6fb02743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789d217af2b17a7981ff4341de893334&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58817a44207e082297ea3faa165db2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb007a78a7e771d39efbeb580b179f2b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624318</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cæsar Simon">
      <data key="d0">Cæsar Simon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Cæsar Simon is Young Simon's cousin, raised by his "big-sis" and "little-sis" after losing his parents, who manifests an imaginative nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Cæsar Simon is the father of Conway, whose background is discussed in the context of family history and inheritance.&lt;SEP&gt;Cæsar Simon is a figure mentioned in relation to a legal dispute regarding his estate and is relevant to Roxie Daymon's legal conversations.&lt;SEP&gt;Cæsar Simon is referenced as a deceased individual whose estate is valued and whose affairs are being discussed by the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Cæsar Simon is a military figure grappling with feelings of betrayal and desertion while reflecting on the consequences of war.&lt;SEP&gt;Cæsar Simon is a character who reflects on the nature of battle and soldiers, expressing disillusionment about conflicting motivations in war.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b703ad46fc561ded805fade2af40be0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec4f8e1bbc32532d2dfcca778eb43e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c11f042f8e301d4f16b51e506f72228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1788abe5b20f786a0ee4558b6fb02743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58817a44207e082297ea3faa165db2bf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624318</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Big-Sis">
      <data key="d0">Big-Sis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Big-Sis is Cæsar Simon's elder sister who took care of him during childhood and provided him with basic needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624318</data>
