    <node id="Steve Brindle">
      <data key="d0">Steve Brindle</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Steve Brindle is a character who shares his background and family history with Conway during their conversation.&lt;SEP&gt;Steve Brindle is a private in the army who treated Cousin Cæsar's wound and has a history of camaraderie with him.&lt;SEP&gt;Steve Brindle is a character who helped carry Cousin Cæsar to safety after he was wounded in battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Steve Brindle is a faithful friend of Cousin Cæsar who is rumored to be mortally wounded during the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Steve Brindle is a soldier in the federal army who is perceived by Cæsar Simon as a coward for deserting.&lt;SEP&gt;Steve Brindle is recognized as a soldier in the federal army, associated with notions of fighting for money.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b703ad46fc561ded805fade2af40be0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec4f8e1bbc32532d2dfcca778eb43e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c11f042f8e301d4f16b51e506f72228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1788abe5b20f786a0ee4558b6fb02743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db12a2e534724a0be9ade4aa8ff10a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58817a44207e082297ea3faa165db2bf</data>
