    <node id="Brain">
      <data key="d0">Brain</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The brain is described as the central telegraph office of the body, responsible for thinking and coordinating bodily functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain processes messages and signals, and its function can be impaired by the consumption of alcohol and tobacco.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain is the central organ of the nervous system that requires pure blood to function effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624485</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerves">
      <data key="d0">Nerves</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Nerves are white cords that connect the brain to the rest of the body, playing a key role in how muscles know when to move.&lt;SEP&gt;Nerves are likened to little white cords that connect the brain to the rest of the body, transmitting messages rapidly.&lt;SEP&gt;Nerves are part of the nervous system, responsible for transmitting signals to and from the brain and are affected by substances like alcohol and tobacco.&lt;SEP&gt;Nerves are part of the nervous system that conveys signals between the brain and body parts, regulating the function of organs, including muscles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1925755a5c65f004018f45749c7912</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624485</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spinal Cord">
      <data key="d0">Spinal Cord</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The spinal cord is a large nerve cord that runs down the spine, serving as a major pathway for information traveling between the brain and the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The spinal cord is a large cord housed within the spine that is part of the nervous system and branches into many nerves.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763624485</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Muscles">
      <data key="d0">Muscles</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Muscles are responsible for movement in the limbs and are associated with the control of bodily motions.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles are responsible for movement in the body and are controlled by the brain's signals.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles are controlled by the nervous system, and their function is impacted by substances that affect the nerves.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles are body tissues that can contract to produce movement, contributing to body strength and locomotion.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles are tissues in the body that facilitate movement, including the movement necessary for breathing and maintaining bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1925755a5c65f004018f45749c7912</data>
