    <node id="Saliva">
      <data key="d0">Saliva</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Saliva is a fluid that mixes with food for preparation and must be spit out after aiding in the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Saliva is a digestive juice in the mouth that begins the process of converting starch into sugar during chewing.&lt;SEP&gt;Saliva is a digestive fluid that plays a role in breaking down starch into sugar during the chewing process.</data>
