    <node id="The Girl">
      <data key="d0">The Girl</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The girl is a young lady dining with Ted, displaying excitement and concern over their situation as runaways.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a character who helps Brice and advises him on how to safely escape after discovering the treasure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a young character who wears a large sunbonnet and is engaged in household tasks at a remote dwelling.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is a young woman, characterized by her singing and her interaction with Fleming regarding the pan and the ring.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a young woman, around seventeen or eighteen years old, who is the daughter of a hunter and shares insights about her family and beliefs with John Fleming.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is characterized as a beautiful child with a stylish appearance, eliciting admiration from Richards, and is the daughter of Senora Ramierez.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-510759579f956294cdeeaa5d655b240a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0516950847d3af3cc640125f4b233d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6bc84603f0e7bd28396f7db8ef2147e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9acbfccf8366a087281ca4b18a20425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1556645e734e01c75f40b96c3891db6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39facf182f4a5fa24e4d960518506e65</data>
