      <data key="d2">Goodwood Plunger refers to Young Harringford's notoriety and identity in the gambling world after his losses and reckless betting behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Goodwood Plunger refers to the nickname given to Young Harringford after his substantial gambling success.&lt;SEP&gt;The Goodwood Plunger is a character who is in distress and reflects upon his troubled relationships while being in Monte Carlo.&lt;SEP&gt;The Goodwood Plunger is a character who interacts with a distressed woman and displays a weary demeanor while discussing gambling.</data>
