      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Miss Trotter">
      <data key="d0">Miss Trotter</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Miss Trotter is a multifaceted character known for her role as a hotel staff member, particularly in the capacity of housekeeper at the Summit Hotel. She is recognized for her observant and practical nature when it comes to her duties, as well as her management of the female staff under her care. This responsibility also places her in a position where she addresses the concerns of others, such as Mr. Calton, with a calm and logical demeanor.

Her interactions extend beyond mere duties; she is portrayed as someone engaged with the emotional and romantic entanglements of the Calton brothers. This involvement reflects her practical common sense and adds dimensions to her character, as she exhibits feelings of impatience and introspection regarding her interactions with others in the sickroom, especially concerning her care for a patient. 

Miss Trotter experiences emotional complexity influenced by the dynamics surrounding the Calton brothers, where her feelings manifest as conflict and anger concerning the decisions affecting their relationships. Her sensitivity is apparent as she offers assistance in these delicate situations. Furthermore, she is curious and concerned about the relationships among other characters, such as her interest in Frida and Chris's interactions.

In her journey, Miss Trotter gains independence and social distinction following Mr. Bilson's marriage, illustrating her growth and adaptability in the face of changing circumstances. Her emotional responses are significant, whether in surprise at Mr. Bilson’s comments, disappointment in missing interactions with the Caltons, or in her inquiries about their well-being. Overall, Miss Trotter embodies a blend of practicality and emotional depth, navigating her roles with a keen awareness of the social intricacies around her.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-369a75ce4a9aaf2cf4882dd927c2352f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343469de09660053c0e80621f41c713b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2949837deae0d2af6b85bc72ecfa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7d20169574265502212f8d8141c5d8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed17775cbe8d000774a8baf77b6324bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d62b651cba5b4535bee8d39106989519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a3a55a4716fe7da650a25825cbe8a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e9467a128fbb05bbbd0b3f83043bf0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34009f4313fe490d580935f9ef87ff52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ef285556657679cada764bf06d06980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d18b6fa9a2e2b728d65fdd7990b785f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625222</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Snapshot Harry">
      <data key="d0">Snapshot Harry</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Snapshot Harry, also known as Henry J. Dimwood, is a complex character who plays a significant role in a narrative concerning family dynamics, crime, and personal influence. He is notably identified as Flo's uncle, which establishes his familial connection and provides context for the relationship between Flo Dimwood and another character, Edward Brice. This relationship facilitates their encounter, marking Harry as a pivotal figure in the unfolding story.

In addition to his familial role, Snapshot Harry is characterized as a highwayman residing in a cabin. His reputation is multifaceted; he exhibits a keen confidence and pride in his skills as a fighter, yet he also serves as an antagonist within the narrative. His involvement in criminal activities, particularly a robbery, positions him at the center of a gang-related issue, highlighting his complex moral standing. His discussions with Brice not only reveal details about the robbery but also showcase his influence over Brice's feelings of guilt and decisions. 

Harry's portrayal extends beyond mere family ties, as he is depicted as a figure of authority and influence, both in his role as an uncle and in his criminal dealings. His interactions and demeanor contribute significantly to the narrative, framing him as a character whose actions resonate with themes of pride, crime, and familial obligation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4e0e93af7a65231c6de3fff16732002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d676579a483a55e2f4c7affcb1119b87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31bf429f0dc25fb5648441a98c5b3697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed354bb280cbffcac2022b4b1028429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05353b2557d1d709496b03e000178076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05f87866de9e32066808684c09b0e143&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cecaf8705a36ced04ac0a85e9fbe1431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7abe56fa54a521b5e22094fb8e7a464b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-877fe45c6401558fe8c7151af1610858&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adcbf578ddc135aad9c7e04e8b9b6a8c</data>
