      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Parkhurst is a perspiring character on the ground who encourages Ned Bray and acknowledges his good character.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is a misogynistic miner who expresses scorn towards the women's involvement in the mining operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is depicted as a foreman who encourages his companions, demonstrating a blend of toughness and camaraderie.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is a character whose discovery leads to excitement among the group and raises questions about his motives.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is a character who interacts with Bray and discusses the meaning of the note Bray found at the spring.</data>
