    <node id="Woodmouse">
      <data key="d0">Woodmouse</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The woodmouse is a character who greets Toto and the raccoon and is addressed for advice regarding brown mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Woodmouse is a character who expresses confusion and is involved in a conversation about troublesome mice and a family wedding.&lt;SEP&gt;The woodmouse is present during the gathering and offers commentary on the dancing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09793d37fba2e0aa20e755731a38abb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c5e6743d54bfa5b3f1b9509aacd347e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625586</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brown Mice">
      <data key="d0">Brown Mice</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Brown mice are described as troublesome and thieving creatures that are relatives of the Woodmouse.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625586</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prick-ear">
      <data key="d0">Prick-ear</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Prick-ear is the son of Woodmouse who is to be married, creating a sense of excitement in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Prick-ear is the son of Mr. Woodmouse, who has a complex relationship with Mr. &lt;DW53&gt; characterized by past conflict and present reconciliation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91c775951405f76d18f8b6972a487cd4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625587</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Cave">
      <data key="d0">The Cave</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Cave is the venue reserved for the wedding of Prick-ear, large enough to accommodate the family connection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cave is the home of the hermit, indicating a secluded living environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a69e187e3b23aa9bc91e07518123699</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625587</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Madam">
      <data key="d0">Madam</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Madam is referenced as a character who has objections to slaughtering other creatures and is influential in the Raccoon and Woodmouse's actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Madam is referenced as a character expected to return to the scene, hinting at her authority in the setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Madam is another companion of Bruin who reacted negatively to the suggestion of eating frog-dumplings.&lt;SEP&gt;Madam is referenced as a grandmother in the conversation, indicating her past beauty and relationship with Toto.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99224c8c1fbad67820c6ae2260eff2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625587</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
