    <node id="Granny">
      <data key="d0">Granny</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Granny is an elderly character deeply engaged in the lives of those around her, particularly Toto and Bruin. She is portrayed as a caring figure, often reflecting on the happy times spent with her companions and expressing grief over Bruin's departure, highlighting her emotional depth and close bonds. 

In her interactions, Granny provides dialogue and suggestions, showcasing her active involvement in conversations with Toto and Bruin. She contributes to preparations for various activities, such as cooking for parties and aiding Baldhead while also expressing concern about Bruin potentially frightening him. This concern extends into her thoughts about the safety of her surroundings, as she is mentioned in the context of an attempted robbery and her possible reactions to it.

Moreover, Granny is noted for her blindness, which adds a unique perspective to her character, as she navigates her relationships and responsibilities despite her visual impairment. Additionally, she is alluded to in the context of Eily’s story, indicating that her influence may extend beyond her direct interactions with Toto and Bruin. Overall, Granny embodies the archetype of a nurturing elder, balancing care, concern, and companionship within her community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b84f4e93e76fa38e1e70383218e0788b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9814d06b58178385c8b7cffd803ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a69e187e3b23aa9bc91e07518123699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-741254ee870941013c032a0acf8e5a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35079c89721b697b8c8d0e998801c8a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24f2b68a542e5127bd458a14221bb2e</data>
