    <node id="King">
      <data key="d0">King</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The King is the father of the Princess, who expresses frustration over her inability to accept marriage proposals.&lt;SEP&gt;The King is a noble who encounters the Princess at his palace and expresses admiration for her beauty and the gems she carries.&lt;SEP&gt;The _king_ is an ancient Chinese musical instrument constructed of slabs of sonorous stone, regarded as sacred and used in religious practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The King is indicated as the person who engaged in a significant hunt that exhausted the horses.&lt;SEP&gt;The King is referenced in relation to Mrs. Crispe's plans regarding godparenting for a child.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03560b66e85f3d2c8750033a19ea401c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-586a7611f02b1deff7ed6b0d6bdd65af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0d3d720b9e8db10b828dd12d97de70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-319e15638832916df6b3c2e9cd3f142c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80d293af5e7df136bc3f73cb98ae3fad</data>
