    <node id="Squirrel">
      <data key="d0">Squirrel</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The Squirrel is depicted as a multifaceted character in various narratives, showcasing both anthropomorphic traits and its role as a small animal in human-centric stories. It demonstrates an engaging personality, displaying an interest in social interactions, notably with characters such as Miss Mary's father, Toto, and the Raccoon. This character initiates conversations, suggesting plans such as tracking down a rat and partaking in events like weddings, allowing for a humorous and lively dynamic in its surroundings.

In addition to these social engagements, the Squirrel plays a pivotal role as a narrator, particularly in assessing the curiosity surrounding the tale of the Red Cow and her lost calf. This narratorial aspect adds depth to its character, depicting it as observant and reflective. Furthermore, the Squirrel participates actively in gatherings and exchanges glances with other forest friends, emphasizing its place within the community of characters.

Visually, the Squirrel is characterized by its charming appearance, often portrayed with a bushy tail, which underscores its confident demeanor. It also exhibits behaviors typical of its species, such as curling up next to a grandmother figure during a nap, blending its animal instincts with human-like social behaviors. Overall, the Squirrel serves as a bridge between the animal and human worlds, enriching the stories with its lively presence and charming interactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-02eb71062b272bf903fae543230157a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d967fb6a3f6684383c4141e9bfb45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b75467e15c21b353927fc372b7848e8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91c4a284dc9ce506ed9cd886b83df824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd1416667b27714cea22c448d2c7894</data>
