    <node id="Eily">
      <data key="d0">Eily</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Eily is a character who interacts with a fairy known as the Green Man and desires to wish for diamonds and pearls.&lt;SEP&gt;Eily is a child who experiences fear and eagerness to explain her actions regarding the appearance of jewels.&lt;SEP&gt;Eily is a character who escapes from a scene of imprisonment and interacts with the Green Man, expressing her distress over a fairy gift.&lt;SEP&gt;Eily is a mortal child who interacts with a fairy and learns about the value of kind words and deeds over material gifts.&lt;SEP&gt;Eily is a character who is finding her voice amidst a situation where she is surrounded by treasures and a woman named Mrs. O'Shaughnessy.&lt;SEP&gt;Eily is a character who, after being mistaken, eventually collects pearls and diamonds and grows up to marry the young Count of Kilmoggan.</data>
