    <node id="Lyre">
      <data key="d0">Lyre</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Lyre is a stringed instrument played with a plectrum and fingers, known for its variation in forms and historical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lyre is a stringed musical instrument historically associated with ancient Hebrews, often depicted in coins from the time of Judas Maccabæus.&lt;SEP&gt;The lyre is a prominent stringed musical instrument in Greek antiquity, commonly associated with beauty and elegance in form.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lyre was a popular stringed instrument in ancient Rome, known for its various forms and significant role in musical performances.&lt;SEP&gt;The lyre is a stringed musical instrument depicted in early Christian art and used in popular pastimes in western Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;The lyre is a stringed musical instrument resembling ancient forms referenced in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Lyre is widely referenced across multiple cultures, including Assyrian, Hebrew, Greek, and Roman contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8e481d0b0dc9178db4c1b9a451a72ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7da70d39d1688e8eb35f0af080c5cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-210eaafae8dea701b360369916174fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7feca07c634684d8111b02a41fcae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ba8bec314d618fd6ba2fced04ef111</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
