    <node id="Arabs">
      <data key="d0">Arabs</data>
      <data key="d1">group</data>
      <data key="d2">The Arabs are a diverse group known for their significant contributions to the development of musical instruments, particularly during the historical period when they introduced various instruments into Spain. This introduction had a lasting impact on the music traditions of Western Europe, showcasing the Arabs as active constructors and innovators in the musical heritage of the region.

In the context of historical conflicts, the Arabs are noted for their involvement in the plundering of Mogador, where they formed alliances with various factions, indicating their strategic role during conflicts. Additionally, the Arabs are referenced in historical accounts pertaining to Castillo Real, which they called "El-Bureeja," highlighting their deep-rooted connection to this location.

Socially, the Arabs, particularly those in Toser, are recognized as local inhabitants engaged in trade and expressing pride in their community, asserting its notable qualities. They are depicted as hardy individuals who interact with locals, suggesting a diverse set of experiences and relationships within their community.

Moreover, the Arabs have been involved in notable political actions, including attacks on the government, showcasing their engagement in broader socio-political events. Overall, the Arabs are characterized by their multifaceted contributions to culture, music, trade, and conflict throughout history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d034b0ebc70d115fe140d386b94caa9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8493bf9cd90b8f6b1a63947e3d6ecb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4512b69e3496f492631c7653788034d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8dad715690b2fe96271b7494f7f290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284546e32da930f297907ef0f48339cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb77c42a6cfd618f0d29c057ae2768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdfdc15ee78020d5a5e9bc96f2c72f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4996254e95ccc6b78afba2bb6b96949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d587eba2d4e09716d8ff298c1f8fad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d3ba708724915d4c95066561027635</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763626536</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Crusaders">
      <data key="d0">Crusaders</data>
      <data key="d1">group</data>
      <data key="d2">The Crusaders played a role in familiarizing Western European nations with eastern musical instruments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Crusaders are depicted as historical figures who procured wood for war machines to assault the Holy City.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d034b0ebc70d115fe140d386b94caa9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2</data>
