    <node id="Musical Instruments">
      <data key="d0">Musical Instruments</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Musical instruments are crucial for understanding the distinctive features of a nation's music and influence the construction of musical compositions.&lt;SEP&gt;Musical instruments are objects used to produce music, greatly varied in design and historical significance across cultures.&lt;SEP&gt;Musical Instruments refer to a variety of devices created for producing music, which is a subject of the discussed handbook.&lt;SEP&gt;Musical instruments encompass various devices used for producing sound, each possessing unique characteristics suitable for different effects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95a9160a14d7266e2100e2d55ebcd715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30e65976acac895df3c3a0c077667c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c92bbb1fd6ed4d39b3fbf9331923c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0658b2c968fe6ee5f181166477508b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4512b69e3496f492631c7653788034d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03c5035205433abd8b211b1d1712aea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f440a8129c9633e91b0a40eef56e62b1</data>
