    <node id="Cymbals">
      <data key="d0">Cymbals</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Egyptian cymbals are similar in shape to modern versions and were found among various ancient artifacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals include the _tzeltzclim_, _metzilloth_, and _metzilth_, referenced within biblical contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals are metallic percussion instruments referenced in the English Bible, distinct from other instruments like the sistrum.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals are counted among the instruments depicted in the Minstrels’ Gallery.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals, also referred to as cymbalum, are percussion instruments noted in musical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c7da70d39d1688e8eb35f0af080c5cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30e65976acac895df3c3a0c077667c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aef18eb73774c5f975cff80e5f2ce51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
