      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Bagpipe, denoted by the term _sumphonia_, may refer to a type of bagpipe as noted by Forkel and others.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bagpipe is a traditional musical instrument known for its ability to produce sound when air is expanded within it, often associated with cultural festivities, particularly in Scotland and Ireland.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bagpipe is another musical instrument represented in the Minstrels’ Gallery.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bagpipe is a wind instrument favored by Celtic and Slavonic cultures, recognized for its distinctive sound and ancient lineage.</data>
