    <node id="Confucius">
      <data key="d0">Confucius</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Confucius was a Chinese philosopher who lived around B.C. 500 and was deeply moved by Chinese music.&lt;SEP&gt;Confucius was an influential Chinese philosopher whose teachings included the desire to be a "wooden-tongued bell of Heaven" to proclaim divine purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0d3d720b9e8db10b828dd12d97de70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afd96cea5225608d5415480cf74f1ac5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625996</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kouei">
      <data key="d0">Kouei</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Kouei is known as the Orpheus of the Chinese, celebrated for his ability to enthrall both animals and humans with music.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0d3d720b9e8db10b828dd12d97de70e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625996</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fohi">
      <data key="d0">Fohi</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Fohi is regarded as the founder of the Chinese empire who lived around B.C. 3000 and is associated with the invention of several stringed instruments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0d3d720b9e8db10b828dd12d97de70e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625996</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Niuva">
      <data key="d0">Niuva</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Niuva is a supernatural female figure in Chinese tradition credited with important musical inventions during Fohi's time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0d3d720b9e8db10b828dd12d97de70e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763625996</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Yu">
      <data key="d0">Yu</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The _yu_ is a type of stone valued for making the _king_, known for its beauty and distinctive sound quality, found in mountain streams.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0d3d720b9e8db10b828dd12d97de70e</data>
