    <node id="Organistrum">
      <data key="d0">Organistrum</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Organistrum is a historical musical instrument considered a predecessor of the hurdy-gurdy, requiring two persons to play.&lt;SEP&gt;The Organistrum is a large string instrument played by two individuals, depicted in an historical ensemble of musicians.&lt;SEP&gt;The Organistrum is a large stringed instrument played by two persons, placed centrally in the depicted group of musicians.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5adf09848918f402d340b581ef777eb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03c5035205433abd8b211b1d1712aea6</data>
