    <node id="Syrinx">
      <data key="d0">Syrinx</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Syrinx, or Pandean pipe, is a musical instrument made up of three to nine tubes and often associated with pastoral music.&lt;SEP&gt;The Syrinx is a historical wind instrument made of tubes tied together, likened to the modern Pandean pipe.&lt;SEP&gt;The Syrinx is a wind instrument illustrated as being played by a musician in the ancient bas-relief.&lt;SEP&gt;The Syrinx is also included in the list of musical instruments depicted in the gallery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5adf09848918f402d340b581ef777eb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03c5035205433abd8b211b1d1712aea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7feca07c634684d8111b02a41fcae1</data>
