      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Camel is an animal vital for transportation and agricultural labor in the context described.&lt;SEP&gt;Camels are animals that can subsist on coarse grass, weeds, and thorns, and are heavily relied upon for transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Camel is a river mentioned as part of the journey to Slaughter Bridge, notable for its historical connection to King Arthur's story.</data>
