    <node id="Muley Suleiman">
      <data key="d0">Muley Suleiman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Muley Suleiman is the late Emperor whose policies regarding the treatment of Jews fluctuate throughout the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman is the uncle of Muley Abd Errahman, who nominated him to the throne based on a dying request.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman is referred to as "The Shereeff of Shereefs," a significant figure in the Shereefian Monarchs of Morocco.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman is a ruler who became Sultan in the early 19th century and was known for maintaining peace and abolishing Christian slavery.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman passed away in 1822.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman is noted as the Sultan of Morocco who confirmed the treaty signed at Fez in 1824.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman is referenced as a historical figure who occasionally resided in Aghla.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-78c973a4a4c99e07c3571a6d29d1779d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feec165bb57c6356de7d23684253d46b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f075dca5ffdfa89a91a9f3f686330e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f75296e95e08ee42b21dc84299286f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67661a5e143ad1775de09087e2149acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2e2382323fa2c2ced43dc3587ea2a6</data>
