    <node id="Sultan">
      <data key="d0">Sultan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Sultan is the ruler at the Maroquine Court whose presence causes the Vizier to panic.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan, referred to as "our Sultan," is the ruler who proposed to marry the Princesse de Conti in accordance with his beliefs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is a ruler who consolidates power in his empire through political maneuvers and authority claims.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is the ruler who must maintain credibility in Fez and control the warparty from the north.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is mentioned as an authority figure who influences the response to requests regarding slavery and abolition.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is referenced as the authority whose engagements restrict local merchants from accompanying the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-680c330ee8036afcbacb673ce690b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97d99746fa60d96d3fbab1f89af585c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd02a45e5de5d4ef105b2b38ed4ab33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2e2382323fa2c2ced43dc3587ea2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0feaae427cf9b154a9a737a238afba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259</data>
