    </node>
    <node id="Rabat">
      <data key="d0">Rabat</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Rabat is a town enclosed by walls, defended on the seaside by forts, and has a significant Jewish population and active merchants.&lt;SEP&gt;Rabat, also called Er-Rabat, is a modern city opposite Salee on the Bouragrag River, noted for its trade and defenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Rabat is a city where various goods are imported and consumed, influencing trade dynamics in Morocco.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac59a77b85c004bd29ffff6b594c7f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d121b85033bc8ae8ffcb392dcbbcf78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
