    <node id="Sheikh Tahid">
      <data key="d0">Sheikh Tahid</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sheikh Tahid is a character mentioned in the text who experiences imprisonment and punishment.&lt;SEP&gt;Sheikh Tahid is a prominent figure in Toser who was imprisoned for not having the tribute ready for the Bey and is said to be wealthy.&lt;SEP&gt;Sheikh Tahid is mentioned in the context of being imprisoned and punished, indicating a significant event related to authority and governance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e8dad715690b2fe96271b7494f7f290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46f6546f0663eb9c1877a5075f89012f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f75296e95e08ee42b21dc84299286f</data>
