    <node id="Mauritania">
      <data key="d0">Mauritania</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Mauritania was a historical region in North Africa, encompassing areas that included parts of modern Morocco and Algeria.&lt;SEP&gt;Mauritania is a historic region related to the origins of the Arabs who invaded Spain.&lt;SEP&gt;Mauritania is a region referenced for its fertility and historical significance, once loosely associated with ancient cities like Lixus.&lt;SEP&gt;Mauritania is described as a fertile country, rich in resources and water bodies, except for a small desert area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73f52bfe54d47067a25b5b0c44706763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac59a77b85c004bd29ffff6b594c7f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cbd510e5f844be534e59040af85f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c31ea51debe67089624a49cd283a6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763626535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Saneeates-Sultan">
      <data key="d0">Saneeates-Sultan</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Saneeates-Sultan, also known as the Garden of the Emperor, is located south of Mogador and is referenced in the context of travel and exploration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33cad941dca515ea1feb8e87a23c7dfb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1763626535</data>
