      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Abd-el-Kader is a revered marabout warrior and representative of the Prophet, idolized by Mussulmen in North Africa, especially Morocco.&lt;SEP&gt;Abd-el-Kader is a marabout warrior revered in North Africa, particularly in Morocco, during the time of hostilities against the Shereefs.&lt;SEP&gt;Abd-el-Kader is referenced as a chief and historical figure associated with military and political influence in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;Abd-el-Kader is an individual who sought refuge among the tribes in the Rif after being compelled to retreat from Algeria.&lt;SEP&gt;Abd-el-Kader is referenced as a historical figure who combines princely and sacerdotal authority in Morocco.&lt;SEP&gt;Abd-el-Kader is referenced as a historical figure whose companions performed rituals during his journey.</data>
