    <node id="Jereed">
      <data key="d0">Jereed</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Jereed is a region in North Africa known for its date plantations and is culturally significant for its inhabitants.&lt;SEP&gt;Jereed is a region where twenty thousand people live on dates for a portion of the year and is characterized by its agricultural practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Jereed is the area where the dates' ripeness was affected by rainfall.&lt;SEP&gt;Jereed refers to a region associated with a quantity of tribute collected, which is difficult to ascertain due to various impediments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Jereed refers to a group or entity involved in the context of tribute comprising goods and animals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f946791371663ec7aa99ab19596abfd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd02a45e5de5d4ef105b2b38ed4ab33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3a1103e1d6efafaf897eb994dbaa44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1030072f07138e17f0700081a9158b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a17fe942d5f36c4709f9e1cb2fc169d3</data>
