    <node id="Hannah">
      <data key="d0">Hannah</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hannah is a character who plays a supportive and emotionally engaged role in her interactions with others, particularly with Noah Topping and Georgiana. She is depicted as someone who expresses concern about relationships and friendships; for instance, she worries about the lack of social connections with Noah. In her new life in St. Marvells, she takes pride in receiving cards from friends, indicating her desire for companionship.

During moments of crisis, such as the situation regarding the missing Dean, Hannah speaks softly to Georgiana, offering reassurance and support. Her character is marked by confidence, especially when she expresses optimism about the eventual safety of Georgiana’s brother. In a poignant scene, Hannah kneels at Georgiana's feet, communicating her commitment to helping bring back her brother safely.

As Hannah transitions into being Mrs. Topping, her relationship with Noah deepens, showcasing her emotional involvement and concern for his well-being. Overall, Hannah serves as a stable and caring figure within her social circle, balancing her own concerns with a strong focus on the welfare of those around her.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de37e70a12227d78dd4e8b830ac40b80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51763246a424f17d012c8a8c92b9dd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9adb1b7231075c5bd3151775f9ce69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59edcbf702bf09e6c7842114ee9fee90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e596e9ce7637f90613b8207baadae53e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5935cd19a49d869dfe9b8b95e3558c7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe1560cf60e9d4a7338b3d121ff45e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdfaa450fecffba6a5f866eaa6aeec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1005fe668029a3498fae762b9e2347d2</data>
