    <node id="Darbey">
      <data key="d0">Darbey</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Darbey is a character depicted as actively participating in various discussions and social interactions, primarily revolving around military matters and the Dean's inquiries. He is engaged in dinner plans alongside the Dean and other characters, showcasing his enthusiasm for these gatherings while portraying a somewhat presumptuous demeanor.

Darbey exhibits a notable interest in music, as he is portrayed as a violinist, which adds another layer to his character. His interactions reveal a rivalry with Major Tarver, suggesting a competitive relationship that may influence his behavior and actions. Additionally, he is depicted as haughty, indicating a sense of superiority that colors his social engagements.

In his role, Darbey extends invitations for social visits, signaling his desire to foster connections with other characters. He is also described as being on duty while guarding the ruins of the "Swan" Inn, indicating a level of responsibility that contrasts with his more casual social interactions. Throughout various scenes, he is often seen sitting in an armchair, a position that signifies his involvement in the unfolding events around him.

Darbey further connects with other characters, as evidenced by his conversation with Sheba, where he expresses a willingness to maintain their friendship, highlighting a more personable trait amidst his presumptuous nature. Overall, Darbey represents a multifaceted character who balances social charm with a competitive spirit and a sense of duty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55bf94783f183c51cfeb7911ef8186ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b102270ef0e98eb298e79412603ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1005fe668029a3498fae762b9e2347d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d690635b31230e7613331edb68d7205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59edcbf702bf09e6c7842114ee9fee90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee051bd08ba32e2c7f5e0938dbbc6c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95bebed720934a7d07e65bb3901bf810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4d7bb5676e6bc4c87b3981f6f0ae16</data>
