    <node id="Salome">
      <data key="d0">Salome</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Salome is a multifaceted character who exhibits a range of emotional responses and interpersonal dynamics in her various interactions. As one of the daughters of the Dean, Salome is deeply concerned about her family’s financial difficulties, often engaging in discussions about their economic status and the need for new clothing. Her concern extends to her father, and she expresses both shock and distress regarding his absence, as well as her feelings related to different situations, including an emotional reaction of anger and disappointment when a ball is canceled due to military duties.

In her relationships, Salome displays tenderness and care for her family members, especially Major Tarver, whom she attends to alongside her father. Her character is also portrayed as lively and playful, taking an active role in dinner preparations and discussions, indicating her youthful spirit. This playfulness is juxtaposed with serious moments where she shows a heightened sense of responsibility, particularly during challenging scenarios, such as managing the household during a fire.

Salome’s social interactions extend to her sister, Sheba, with whom she collaborates to seek assistance from their aunt, reflecting her desire to navigate difficulties together. Additionally, her curiosity about her family’s history is evident in her conversations about Georgiana Tidman, her aunt, and the lineage of yearlings in the racing context, showcasing her youthful inquisitiveness and emotional engagement with her family's past.

Salome is consistently depicted as a character with depth, demonstrating both concern for her loved ones and an eagerness to participate actively in familial and social activities. Her role encapsulates a blend of youthful exuberance and serious reflections, making her a significant figure within her narrative context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-55bf94783f183c51cfeb7911ef8186ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51763246a424f17d012c8a8c92b9dd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbd76b6f2049550600c7b5f2e214524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b102270ef0e98eb298e79412603ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd7991bf11c9a900752c7c353a0990c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1005fe668029a3498fae762b9e2347d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea62626f9134cd6522f82d474b2c357b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d690635b31230e7613331edb68d7205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3c3f1e54f2cd94a7ba1914df2ac61e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39786c205992e5e0d95dca55454814f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af1eb7dd19180841d20fad29810d6539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95bebed720934a7d07e65bb3901bf810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b0199cb2086a0bf36a1dde1fbe62d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4d7bb5676e6bc4c87b3981f6f0ae16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2c82e11dcce129d5615a4deb4b0724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdfaa450fecffba6a5f866eaa6aeec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-797a0e01fc6bbbd28cfe260a566d2a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee051bd08ba32e2c7f5e0938dbbc6c85</data>
