    <node id="Sheba">
      <data key="d0">Sheba</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sheba is a multifaceted character, identified primarily as the sister of Salome. Sheba portrays a playful yet dramatic demeanor as she engages in various actions and dialogues, particularly in the context of their evening preparations. While she exhibits curiosity and emotional responses to her Aunt Georgiana Tidman's return, she also faces familial challenges, expressing grief over financial difficulties and their urgent need for clothing.

Sheba's interactions extend beyond her sister, as she is described as another niece of Georgiana, actively participating in conversations regarding family matters and their father's financial woes. Sheba expresses a desire to win money through horse racing, depicting her ambition and awareness of the family's economic situation.

In the context of the narrative, Sheba reveals a complex emotional landscape. She shares poignant moments with Salome regarding their father, reflecting on their shared experiences of skepticism about marriage and expressing annoyance with their circumstances. Additionally, Sheba communicates with others about their plans and exhibits a certain overconfidence, indicating her strong personality within group dynamics that include characters like Blore and Salome.

Throughout various scenes, Sheba is not only involved in discussions of significant issues, such as military obligations and revenge, but she also actively defends herself and Salome, asserting their trustworthiness. Her character provides depth to the story, contributing to the discussions around financial troubles and showcasing a desire for contemplation regarding her relationships with others.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51763246a424f17d012c8a8c92b9dd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbd76b6f2049550600c7b5f2e214524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b102270ef0e98eb298e79412603ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd7991bf11c9a900752c7c353a0990c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1005fe668029a3498fae762b9e2347d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea62626f9134cd6522f82d474b2c357b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d690635b31230e7613331edb68d7205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3c3f1e54f2cd94a7ba1914df2ac61e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39786c205992e5e0d95dca55454814f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59edcbf702bf09e6c7842114ee9fee90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3037df50481adaea6024d7ae1774bd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af1eb7dd19180841d20fad29810d6539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee051bd08ba32e2c7f5e0938dbbc6c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b0199cb2086a0bf36a1dde1fbe62d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4d7bb5676e6bc4c87b3981f6f0ae16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2c82e11dcce129d5615a4deb4b0724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdfaa450fecffba6a5f866eaa6aeec0</data>
