      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Penzance is a nearby town in Cornwall mentioned as a destination for the narrator's planned journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Penzance is a nearby town to St. Michael's Mount, known for its genteel atmosphere and civilised charm.&lt;SEP&gt;Penzance is a town in Cornwall that is referenced during the journey towards St. Ives.&lt;SEP&gt;Penzance is a lovely neighbourhood known for its rich vegetation, cottage-gardens, and scenic views of the coastline.&lt;SEP&gt;Penzance is a town in Cornwall characterized by its rich vegetation and beautiful roads.&lt;SEP&gt;Penzance is mentioned as a destination reached by the narrator, significant for its connection to the day's events.</data>
