    <node id="St. Michael's Mount">
      <data key="d0">St. Michael's Mount</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">St. Michael's Mount is a notable location featured in the illustrations of "An Unsentimental Journey Through Cornwall."&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a landmark opposite Marazion, prominent in the narrative as a scenic point of interest.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a rocky island in Cornwall, England, known for its medieval fortress and fishing village at its base.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is an island in Cornwall featuring a historic site and a castle, appearing as a focal point in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a notable landmark near Marazion, where the princess and her party are expected to visit.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is highlighted as a visual feature shining in the sunset, showcasing natural beauty.</data>
