      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Cadgwith is a location that is included in Charles's plan to drive the ladies after visiting Kennack Sands.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadgwith is a fishing village in Cornwall known for its natural beauty and coastal views.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadgwith is a fishing-village noted for its picturesque environment and mild climate.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadgwith is a destination where visitors go for walks, mentioned in connection with Kynance.&lt;SEP&gt;Cadgwith is the location to which John Curgenven and other fishermen rowed to bring survivors ashore during the shipwreck.</data>
