    <node id="Charles">
      <data key="d0">Charles</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Charles is a multifaceted character who plays various supportive roles during journeys and excursions in the narrative. He is primarily depicted as a young carriage driver, characterized by his bright appearance and a teetotaler background, possibly linked to family struggles with alcohol. This aspect may contribute to his reliability and thoughtful nature throughout the journeys.

Charles engages with his companions in meaningful conversation, such as discussions about blackberries, and reflects on personal loss. He exhibits a deep concern for the safety and comfort of those in his company, acting as a guide and providing direction, especially during trips in Cornwall. His knowledge of local attractions, such as Cadgwith—described as a charming winter residence—further establishes him as a resourceful character.

He is also portrayed as a faithful companion, showcasing kindness towards his horse and friends while actively participating in the practical aspects of travel. Whether transporting travelers or ensuring their safety during excursions, Charles proves to be both considerate and practical. He is involved in many aspects of the journey, from proposing boating trips to providing encouragement and advice during cave explorations.

In addition to these roles, Charles is depicted as Mary Mundy's brother, linking him to personal interactions within the narrative. He is seen patiently waiting in front of a blacksmith's shop and displaying an active interest in the itinerary and well-being of his companions, which highlights his considerate nature. Ultimately, Charles is presented as a dedicated character who facilitates travel experiences, offering both practical support and emotional comfort to the narrator and fellow travelers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4b37d7eb87d239e5e28288c02a976c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38519f656227a2cd39eb8d1b1d316bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0acdfa773f8af706f91ebb20b7581863&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9567484ec2e94de37ab803e0df4f01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66d2ddcb0f1123cca7b29268a9a9c19f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-954cde81659c45a63d9688ff1660cf5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4b3e608aee39b08d0a23ee7e08f470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c7f8bd62dafa63c78ea529b3f1857b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe99e4059d4a83bdd69b8d710ad9ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0ed1717208ea935e1a0b9a0b5345925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32469f057cd19090b7cd1fecfc96b839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88bb0742ed8d4804fc66811c924845ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad935363bd1f002bacc611b031c99cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d970d400c7e2e3d42bc4de363f798b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87bd881119189a688bfde0ea81ce77c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9947d8e5a23dab49c88d36cae1db57a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a287228f598fefb3952d1a82454d23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-529c2631117811cb886077fba9841146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f749ef842a6b7afcee9121c9350e439&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de865f683f08a0b7587135564fd925d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-515ede8184a7b2fd3887b2b0ba59654d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d3595409ddcf313d3ede9dd4bc5229e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b07f91a63f12116362cc5c772cacd1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2731c78f5f53bb6ab7e2954c093064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a2a56cdb0d2952e81ef8205b9a6709a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
