    <node id="Kynance">
      <data key="d0">Kynance</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Kynance is a coastal location situated near the Lizard in Cornwall, England. It is prominently associated with the coast-guard service and is recognized for its picturesque scenery and charming shore, making it a significant destination for visitors. Known for its scenic bathing establishments, Kynance attracts individuals seeking leisure and recreation along its coastline.

The location is also noted for specific tide conditions that may affect the timing of visits, emphasizing its dynamic interaction with the sea. Kynance is mentioned as a place from which to enjoy distant views, particularly seen from Housel Cove, thereby underscoring its geographical and aesthetic importance.

Additionally, Kynance is depicted as a route for visitors traveling on foot from the Lizard, indicating its accessibility and appeal to walkers and tourists. John Curgenven offers to guide ladies to Kynance, highlighting its status as a notable destination within the coastal features of the area. 

The region is further associated with Kynance Sands, which adds to its relevance in the broader narrative of coastal exploration and tourism. Visitors to Kynance can expect to hear the calming sound of waves during quiet nights, enhancing the location's charm and atmosphere for those drawn to its natural beauty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4b37d7eb87d239e5e28288c02a976c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c397e03eded0bedcfd22c948ef8967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-954cde81659c45a63d9688ff1660cf5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b147dfcab79c75ec8a9092c688ad363d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9744909492c02bf3c9b5f954e5e18588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de865f683f08a0b7587135564fd925d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801fd5542928b9ae42e3b1c8871af597&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d3595409ddcf313d3ede9dd4bc5229e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a2a56cdb0d2952e81ef8205b9a6709a</data>
