    <node id="King Arthur">
      <data key="d0">King Arthur</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">King Arthur is a legendary monarch central to British folklore, renowned for his heroism and quest for justice. He is portrayed as the ideal knight, embodying noble virtues such as bravery and honor, often compared to figures like Jack the Giantkiller for these character traits. His story is imbued with themes of love and betrayal, linking him to many tales within the broader narrative of Arthurian legend.

King Arthur is prominently associated with Tintagel, a site that is said to be his birthplace. This connection to Cornwall's folklore positions him within a rich tapestry of myths that celebrate his legacy. Additionally, Arthur serves as a historical reference point regarding locations such as the Lizard Lights, showcasing how his legend intertwines with geographical elements of the British landscape.

He is also recognized for his leadership of the Knights of the Round Table, a fellowship renowned for their valiant endeavors. The sword Excalibur is a significant artifact often linked to him, symbolizing his right to rule and his heroic strength. Through these associations, King Arthur remains a timeless figure representing ideals of chivalry and justice, highlighting the enduring nature of his legend in literature and culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-322cff857c0beb5c471bdf49a8426f1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c1cd94b8b0a4c57576d20936affb7f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ea591b9bece4549c4c0df1e1172759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b244aae51773bf1f2438d4305c91ceec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40a925861c89aa50e0fdf703fdaf56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f67bf042c7366daa951d89bffb75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b07f91a63f12116362cc5c772cacd1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64b7ad3d05ef11eb080f1a8e10aa6ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14dbef413cc17a6b6cd1e7d1b659eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2731c78f5f53bb6ab7e2954c093064</data>
