    <edge source="Mr. Bilson" target="Miss Trotter">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation between Miss Trotter and Mr. Bilson encompasses a professional yet intricate dynamic that evolves over time. Miss Trotter, who works under Mr. Bilson at the Summit Hotel, is aware of the circumstances surrounding Mr. Calton's potential wealth, indicating her perceptiveness and relevance in the hotel’s operations. She acknowledges Mr. Bilson's authority as her employer while maintaining a professional demeanor throughout their interactions.

Mr. Bilson, in turn, expresses gratitude toward Miss Trotter for her assistance and the care she has shown to his guests, which reflects a level of appreciation for her dedication and competence. Following his announcement of marriage to Miss Jansen, Mr. Bilson assures Miss Trotter of her continued position at the hotel, demonstrating a commitment to her role despite his changing personal life. Notably, he promotes her to take full control of the Summit Hotel after his marriage, signifying a significant shift in her responsibilities and the trust he places in her capabilities.

The relationship between Miss Trotter and Mr. Bilson also encompasses a deeper emotional complexity. Mr. Bilson reveals feelings of regret and emotional vulnerabilities to Miss Trotter, leading to reflective exchanges that reveal their sentiments toward one another. Miss Trotter, in seeking emotional understanding from Mr. Bilson, adds tension to their relationship, as they navigate their feelings amidst changing circumstances.

A pivotal moment occurs when Miss Trotter resigns, coinciding with Mr. Bilson's return, which marks a notable change in management at the Summit Hotel. This resignation may suggest underlying tensions or unresolved issues in their relationship, further complicating their professional and personal dynamics. Overall, the relationship between Miss Trotter and Mr. Bilson is characterized by a blend of professionalism, emotional depth, and significant transitions within their respective roles and feelings towards each other.</data>
